window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2"]={"id":"CGL-14-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2","title":"CGL 14 OCT 2026 SHIFT 2","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000074181","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"A sum triples in 8 years at simple interest. Find the rate per annum. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक राशि साधारण ब्याज पर 8 वर्षों में तिगुनी हो जाती है। प्रति वर्ष दर ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"25%"},"2":{"en":"33%"},"3":{"en":"50%"},"4":{"en":"15%"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Tripling means the interest equals twice the principal, i.e. P × R × 8 / 100 = 2P<br>So 8R = 200 and R = 25%<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 25%.</b>","hi":"तिगुनी होने का अर्थ ब्याज मूलधन का दोगुना है, अर्थात P × R × 8 / 100 = 2P<br>अतः 8R = 200 और R = 25%<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 25% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000074182","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"What is the next number in the series?<br>2, 6, 12, 20, 30, ? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"श्रेणी में अगली संख्या क्या है?<br>2, 6, 12, 20, 30, ? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"36"},"2":{"en":"42"},"3":{"en":"38"},"4":{"en":"40"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The terms are n(n + 1) for n = 1, 2, 3, 4, 5: 1·2 = 2, 2·3 = 6, 3·4 = 12, 4·5 = 20, 5·6 = 30<br>Next term = 6 × 7 = 42<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 42.</b>","hi":"पद n(n + 1) के रूप में हैं जहाँ n = 1, 2, 3, 4, 5: 1·2 = 2, 2·3 = 6, 3·4 = 12, 4·5 = 20, 5·6 = 30<br>अगला पद = 6 × 7 = 42<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 42 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000074183","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"GRAPE\" is written as \"IUCSG\". How will \"APPLE\" be written in the same code language? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"किसी निश्चित कूट भाषा में \"GRAPE\" को \"IUCSG\" लिखा जाता है। उसी कूट भाषा में \"APPLE\" को कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"CSROG"},"2":{"en":"CRSOG"},"3":{"en":"GSROC"},"4":{"en":"GRSOC"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The shifts alternate by two and three places: G→I (+2), R→U (+3), A→C (+2), P→S (+3), E→G (+2)<br>APPLE gives A→C, P→S, P→R, L→O, E→G<br>Code = CSROG<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): CSROG.</b>","hi":"स्थानांतरण बारी-बारी दो और तीन स्थान का है: G→I (+2), R→U (+3), A→C (+2), P→S (+3), E→G (+2)<br>APPLE से A→C, P→S, P→R, L→O, E→G<br>कूट = CSROG<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): CSROG है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000074184","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Direction: Study the statement and determine which of the given conclusions logically follows.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>The city administration expanded public Wi-Fi services after surveys indicated increasing digital service usage among commuters in transportation hubs.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. Every commuter uses digital services regularly.<br>II. Public Wi-Fi services completely replace mobile internet networks. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निर्देश: कथन का अध्ययन कीजिए और निर्धारित कीजिए कि दिए गए निष्कर्षों में से कौन-सा तार्किक रूप से निकलता है।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>परिवहन केंद्रों पर यात्रियों में डिजिटल सेवाओं के बढ़ते उपयोग के सर्वेक्षण संकेत मिलने के बाद नगर प्रशासन ने सार्वजनिक वाई-फ़ाई सेवाएँ बढ़ाईं।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. प्रत्येक यात्री नियमित रूप से डिजिटल सेवाओं का उपयोग करता है।<br>II. सार्वजनिक वाई-फ़ाई सेवाएँ मोबाइल इंटरनेट नेटवर्क का पूर्णतः स्थान ले लेती हैं। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I follows","hi":"केवल I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Only II follows","hi":"केवल II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Both follow","hi":"दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither follows","hi":"कोई नहीं निकलता"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"'Increasing usage' does not mean that every commuter uses digital services, so I is too broad<br>The statement never says that Wi-Fi replaces mobile internet, so II is unsupported<br>Hence neither conclusion follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Neither follows.</b>","hi":"'बढ़ता उपयोग' का अर्थ यह नहीं कि प्रत्येक यात्री डिजिटल सेवाओं का उपयोग करता है, अतः I अति व्यापक है<br>कथन कहीं नहीं कहता कि वाई-फ़ाई मोबाइल इंटरनेट का स्थान ले लेती है, अतः II आधारहीन है<br>इसलिए कोई भी निष्कर्ष नहीं निकलता<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): कोई नहीं निकलता है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000074185","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"A train 240 m long crosses another train 360 m long moving in the opposite direction in 12 seconds. If the speed of the first train is 54 km/h, what is the speed of the second train? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"240 मीटर लंबी एक रेलगाड़ी विपरीत दिशा में चल रही 360 मीटर लंबी दूसरी रेलगाड़ी को 12 सेकंड में पार करती है। यदि पहली रेलगाड़ी की चाल 54 किमी/घंटा है, तो दूसरी रेलगाड़ी की चाल क्या है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"108 km/h","hi":"108 किमी/घंटा"},"2":{"en":"126 km/h","hi":"126 किमी/घंटा"},"3":{"en":"144 km/h","hi":"144 किमी/घंटा"},"4":{"en":"162 km/h","hi":"162 किमी/घंटा"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Total distance = 240 + 360 = 600 m and relative speed = \\(\\frac{600}{12}=50\\) m/s = 50 × 3.6 = 180 km/h<br>So 54 + speed of the second train = 180<br>Speed of the second train = 126 km/h<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 126 km/h.</b>","hi":"कुल दूरी = 240 + 360 = 600 मीटर तथा सापेक्ष चाल = \\(\\frac{600}{12}=50\\) मीटर/सेकंड = 50 × 3.6 = 180 किमी/घंटा<br>अतः 54 + दूसरी रेलगाड़ी की चाल = 180<br>दूसरी रेलगाड़ी की चाल = 126 किमी/घंटा<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 126 किमी/घंटा है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000074186","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"Choose the option that perfectly matches the given address.<br><br><b>Original Address:</b><br>Residence Unit–IX/27The Eminence Royale, Phase–ⅢMahatma Gandhi Rd. ExtensionPuducherry 605001India [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"वह विकल्प चुनिए जो दिए गए पते से पूर्णतः मेल खाता है।<br><br><b>मूल पता:</b><br>Residence Unit–IX/27The Eminence Royale, Phase–ⅢMahatma Gandhi Rd. ExtensionPuducherry 605001India [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Residence Unit–IX/27The Eminenc Royale, Phase ⅢMahatma Gandhi Rd. ExtensionPuducherry 605001India"},"2":{"en":"Residence Unit-IX/27The Eminence Royale, Phase–ⅢMahatma Gandhi Rd,ExtensionPuducherry 605001India"},"3":{"en":"Residence Unit–IX/27The Eminence Royale. Phase–IIIMahatma Gandhi Rd. ExtensionPuducherry 605001India"},"4":{"en":"Residence Unit–IX/27The Eminence Royale, Phase–ⅢMahatma Gandhi Rd. ExtensionPuducherry 605001India"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Option 1 writes “Eminenc” for “Eminence” and drops the dash in “Phase Ⅲ”<br>Option 2 uses a short hyphen in “Unit-IX” and a comma in place of the full stop after “Rd”<br>Option 3 puts a full stop after “Royale” and writes “III” as three separate letters<br>Only option 4 matches the original exactly<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Residence Unit–IX/27The Eminence Royale, Phase–ⅢMahatma Gandhi Rd. ExtensionPuducherry 605001India.</b>","hi":"विकल्प 1 में “Eminence” के स्थान पर “Eminenc” है और “Phase Ⅲ” में डैश नहीं है<br>विकल्प 2 में “Unit-IX” में छोटा हाइफ़न है और “Rd” के बाद पूर्ण विराम के स्थान पर अल्पविराम है<br>विकल्प 3 में “Royale” के बाद पूर्ण विराम है और “III” तीन अलग अक्षरों में लिखा है<br>केवल विकल्प 4 मूल पते से पूर्णतः मेल खाता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): Residence Unit–IX/27The Eminence Royale, Phase–ⅢMahatma Gandhi Rd. ExtensionPuducherry 605001India है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000074187","section":"REASONING","topic":"Missing Number","question":{"en":"In the following question, a matrix of numbers is given. These numbers follow a certain pattern either row-wise or column-wise. Identify this pattern and choose the missing number accordingly.<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">50</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">11</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में संख्याओं का एक आव्यूह दिया गया है। ये संख्याएँ पंक्ति-वार या स्तंभ-वार किसी निश्चित पैटर्न का पालन करती हैं। इस पैटर्न को पहचानिए और उसके अनुसार लुप्त संख्या चुनिए।<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">50</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">11</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"21"},"2":{"en":"33"},"3":{"en":"40"},"4":{"en":"11"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Column-wise, the bottom number = third row × second row − first row<br>Column I: 9 × 6 − 4 = 50 ✔ and column II: 2 × 7 − 3 = 11 ✔<br>Missing number = 8 × 2 − 5 = 11<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 11.</b>","hi":"स्तंभ-वार सबसे नीचे की संख्या = तीसरी पंक्ति × दूसरी पंक्ति − पहली पंक्ति<br>स्तंभ I: 9 × 6 − 4 = 50 ✔ तथा स्तंभ II: 2 × 7 − 3 = 11 ✔<br>लुप्त संख्या = 8 × 2 − 5 = 11<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 11 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000074188","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"If P ÷ Q means P is the father of Q; P * Q means P is the mother of Q; P + Q means P is the brother of Q; P - Q means P is the sister of Q, how is S related to T in the expression 'S + R ÷ V - T'? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि P ÷ Q का अर्थ P, Q का पिता है; P * Q का अर्थ P, Q की माता है; P + Q का अर्थ P, Q का भाई है; P - Q का अर्थ P, Q की बहन है, तो व्यंजक 'S + R ÷ V - T' में S का T से क्या संबंध है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Paternal Uncle","hi":"चाचा"},"2":{"en":"Brother","hi":"भाई"},"3":{"en":"Father","hi":"पिता"},"4":{"en":"Nephew","hi":"भतीजा"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"293\" height=\"134\" viewBox=\"0 0 293 134\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><g fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"><rect x=\"88\" y=\"34\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"185\" y=\"88\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/></g><path d=\"M173 54V76M150 76H195M150 76V88M195 76V88M101 24H173M101 24V34M173 24V34\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"101\" y=\"48\">S+</text><text x=\"173\" y=\"48\">R+</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"102\">V−</text><text x=\"195\" y=\"102\">T</text></g><text x=\"146\" y=\"129\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text></svg><br>S is the brother of T's father R, so S is T's paternal uncle.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Paternal Uncle.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"293\" height=\"134\" viewBox=\"0 0 293 134\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><g fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"><rect x=\"88\" y=\"34\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"185\" y=\"88\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/></g><path d=\"M173 54V76M150 76H195M150 76V88M195 76V88M101 24H173M101 24V34M173 24V34\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"101\" y=\"48\">S+</text><text x=\"173\" y=\"48\">R+</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"102\">V−</text><text x=\"195\" y=\"102\">T</text></g><text x=\"146\" y=\"129\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+ पुरुष  − स्त्री  — भाई-बहन  = पति-पत्नी  | पीढ़ी</text></svg><br>S, T के पिता R का भाई है, अतः S, T का चाचा है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): चाचा है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000074189","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Which of the following centre code does not follow the pattern of \"two uppercase letters followed by their reverse alphabetical order\"? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा केंद्र कूट \"दो बड़े अक्षरों के बाद उनका विपरीत वर्णमाला क्रम\" के पैटर्न का पालन नहीं करता? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"ABBA"},"2":{"en":"CDDC"},"3":{"en":"EFGF"},"4":{"en":"GHHG"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"In ABBA, CDDC and GHHG the second pair is the reverse of the first pair (AB→BA, CD→DC, GH→HG)<br>In EFGF the first pair is EF, so the reverse should be FE, but it is GF<br>Hence EFGF does not follow the pattern<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): EFGF.</b>","hi":"ABBA, CDDC तथा GHHG में दूसरा युग्म पहले युग्म का उलटा है (AB→BA, CD→DC, GH→HG)<br>EFGF में पहला युग्म EF है, अतः उलटा FE होना चाहिए, परंतु यहाँ GF है<br>इसलिए EFGF पैटर्न का पालन नहीं करता<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): EFGF है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000074190","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"During a team lunch, a colleague who is fasting for religious reasons politely declines food. Another team member makes repeated jokes about their choice, claiming they are \"just teasing.\" What is the most professional and respectful way to handle this situation? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"टीम लंच के दौरान एक सहकर्मी धार्मिक कारणों से व्रत रखते हुए विनम्रता से भोजन लेने से मना कर देता है। दूसरा टीम सदस्य उनकी पसंद पर बार-बार मज़ाक करता है और कहता है कि वह \"बस छेड़ रहा है\"। इस स्थिति को संभालने का सबसे व्यावसायिक और सम्मानजनक तरीका क्या है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Calmly remind the team that all individual religious practices and personal choices should be fully respected.","hi":"शांति से टीम को याद दिलाएँ कि सभी व्यक्तिगत धार्मिक प्रथाओं और व्यक्तिगत पसंदों का पूर्ण सम्मान होना चाहिए।"},"2":{"en":"Participate by laughing along with the jokes to keep the atmosphere light and comfortable for everyone.","hi":"माहौल हल्का और सहज बनाए रखने के लिए मज़ाक में साथ हँसें।"},"3":{"en":"Choose to do absolutely nothing unless the colleague who is fasting specifically complains about the behavior.","hi":"जब तक व्रत रखने वाला सहकर्मी स्वयं शिकायत न करे, तब तक कुछ न करें।"},"4":{"en":"Advise the colleague who is fasting that they should simply ignore the jokes to avoid creating tension.","hi":"व्रत रखने वाले सहकर्मी को सलाह दें कि वे तनाव से बचने के लिए मज़ाक अनदेखा कर दें।"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Repeated jokes on a religious practice make the workplace uncomfortable for a colleague, so silence or joining the laughter supports the wrong behaviour<br>A calm reminder that personal and religious choices must be respected corrects the atmosphere without humiliating anyone<br>Asking the colleague to ignore the jokes puts the burden on the person who is already being teased<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Calmly remind the team that all individual religious practices and personal choices should be fully respected.</b>","hi":"धार्मिक प्रथा पर बार-बार मज़ाक सहकर्मी के लिए कार्यस्थल को असहज बनाता है, अतः चुप रहना या हँसी में शामिल होना गलत व्यवहार को समर्थन देना है<br>शांति से यह याद दिलाना कि व्यक्तिगत और धार्मिक पसंद का सम्मान होना चाहिए, किसी का अपमान किए बिना वातावरण सुधारता है<br>सहकर्मी से मज़ाक अनदेखा करने को कहना उसी व्यक्ति पर बोझ डालना है जिसे छेड़ा जा रहा है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): शांति से टीम को याद दिलाएँ कि सभी व्यक्तिगत धार्मिक प्रथाओं और व्यक्तिगत पसंदों का पूर्ण सम्मान होना चाहिए। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000074191","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"Choose the option which is exactly similar to: 04-03-2026, 55-C, Vidhan Sabha Marg, Hazratganj, Lucknow-226001 [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"उस विकल्प का चयन कीजिए जो इससे पूर्णतः समान है: 04-03-2026, 55-C, Vidhan Sabha Marg, Hazratganj, Lucknow-226001 [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"04-03-2026, 55-C, Vidhan Sabha Marg, Hazratganj, Lucknow-226001"},"2":{"en":"04-03-2026, 55-E, Vidhan Sabha Marg, Hazratganj, Lucknow-226001"},"3":{"en":"04-03-2025, 55-C, Vidhan Sabha Marg, Hazratganj, Lucknow-226001"},"4":{"en":"03-04-2026, 55-C, Vidhan Sabha Marg, Hazratganj, Lucknow-226001"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Option 2 changes 55-C to 55-E, option 3 changes the year to 2025 and option 4 interchanges the day and the month<br>Only option 1 repeats the date, the house number, the area and the PIN exactly<br>So option 1 is exactly similar to the given address<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 04-03-2026, 55-C, Vidhan Sabha Marg, Hazratganj, Lucknow-226001.</b>","hi":"विकल्प 2 में 55-C के स्थान पर 55-E है, विकल्प 3 में वर्ष 2025 है और विकल्प 4 में दिन तथा माह बदल दिए गए हैं<br>केवल विकल्प 1 तारीख, मकान संख्या, क्षेत्र तथा पिन ठीक दोहराता है<br>अतः विकल्प 1 दिए पते से पूर्णतः समान है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 04-03-2026, 55-C, Vidhan Sabha Marg, Hazratganj, Lucknow-226001 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000074192","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter/Alphabetical Analogy","question":{"en":"What should come in place of question mark (?) in the following analogy?<br>EJO : TYD :: INS : ? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित सादृश्य में प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर क्या आएगा?<br>EJO : TYD :: INS : ? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"WCH"},"2":{"en":"XCG"},"3":{"en":"XCH"},"4":{"en":"XBH"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Each letter of EJO moves 15 places forward: E(5)→T(20), J(10)→Y(25), O(15)→D(30−26=4)<br>Applying +15 to INS: I(9)→X(24), N(14)→C(29−26=3), S(19)→H(34−26=8)<br>So the answer is XCH<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): XCH.</b>","hi":"EJO का प्रत्येक अक्षर 15 स्थान आगे जाता है: E(5)→T(20), J(10)→Y(25), O(15)→D(30−26=4)<br>INS पर +15 लगाने से: I(9)→X(24), N(14)→C(29−26=3), S(19)→H(34−26=8)<br>अतः उत्तर XCH है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): XCH है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000074193","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"In the given question, a few statements have been given followed by conclusions based on them. Consider the statements to be true and answer which of the given conclusions logically follow the statement.<br><b>Statements</b><br>1. All diamonds are gems.<br>2. Some gems are synthetic.<br>3. No synthetic material is biodegradable.<br><b>Conclusions</b><br>I. Some diamonds may be synthetic.<br>II. No biodegradable material is a gem.<br>III. Some gems are not biodegradable.<br>IV. All diamonds are biodegradable. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दिए गए प्रश्न में कुछ कथन और उनके आधार पर निष्कर्ष दिए गए हैं। कथनों को सत्य मानिए और बताइए कि दिए गए निष्कर्षों में से कौन-से तार्किक रूप से कथन का अनुसरण करते हैं।<br><b>कथन</b><br>1. सभी हीरे रत्न हैं।<br>2. कुछ रत्न कृत्रिम हैं।<br>3. कोई भी कृत्रिम पदार्थ जैव-अपघटनीय नहीं है।<br><b>निष्कर्ष</b><br>I. कुछ हीरे कृत्रिम हो सकते हैं।<br>II. कोई भी जैव-अपघटनीय पदार्थ रत्न नहीं है।<br>III. कुछ रत्न जैव-अपघटनीय नहीं हैं।<br>IV. सभी हीरे जैव-अपघटनीय हैं। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I and III follow","hi":"केवल I और III अनुसरण करते हैं"},"2":{"en":"Only II and III follow","hi":"केवल II और III अनुसरण करते हैं"},"3":{"en":"Only III follows","hi":"केवल III अनुसरण करता है"},"4":{"en":"Only I, II and III follow","hi":"केवल I, II और III अनुसरण करते हैं"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The synthetic gems may overlap with diamonds, so 'some diamonds may be synthetic' is a valid possibility and I follows<br>Gems that are synthetic are surely not biodegradable, so some gems are not biodegradable and III follows<br>No biodegradable material is a gem is too strong and IV contradicts statement 3, so II and IV do not follow<br>Hence only I and III follow<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only I and III follow.</b>","hi":"कृत्रिम रत्न हीरों से अतिव्यापी हो सकते हैं, अतः 'कुछ हीरे कृत्रिम हो सकते हैं' वैध संभावना है और I अनुसरण करता है<br>कृत्रिम रत्न निश्चित रूप से जैव-अपघटनीय नहीं हैं, अतः कुछ रत्न जैव-अपघटनीय नहीं हैं और III अनुसरण करता है<br>'कोई भी जैव-अपघटनीय पदार्थ रत्न नहीं है' अति है तथा IV कथन 3 का विरोध करता है, अतः II और IV अनुसरण नहीं करते<br>इसलिए केवल I और III अनुसरण करते हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल I और III अनुसरण करते हैं है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000074194","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"A teacher notices that one student is doing most of the work in a group project while other team members contribute very little. To demonstrate pedagogical leadership, encourage collaborative conflict resolution, and constructively understand the root cause of the unequal participation, what is the best action for the teacher to take? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक शिक्षक देखता है कि समूह परियोजना में एक विद्यार्थी अधिकांश कार्य कर रहा है जबकि अन्य सदस्य बहुत कम योगदान दे रहे हैं। शैक्षणिक नेतृत्व दिखाने, सहयोगपूर्ण विवाद समाधान को प्रोत्साहित करने तथा असमान भागीदारी के मूल कारण को रचनात्मक ढंग से समझने के लिए शिक्षक को सबसे अच्छा क्या करना चाहिए? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Facilitate a supportive discussion with the entire group to review task allocation and discover why contribution levels are unequal.","hi":"पूरे समूह के साथ सहायक चर्चा कराएँ जिसमें कार्य-विभाजन की समीक्षा हो और यह पता चले कि योगदान का स्तर असमान क्यों है।"},"2":{"en":"Publicly humiliate the inactive students in front of the classroom to force them into working.","hi":"निष्क्रिय विद्यार्थियों का कक्षा के सामने सार्वजनिक रूप से अपमान करें ताकि वे काम करने पर विवश हों।"},"3":{"en":"Ignore the imbalance completely and assign the exact same grade to all members without any intervention.","hi":"असंतुलन को पूरी तरह अनदेखा करें और बिना किसी हस्तक्षेप के सभी सदस्यों को समान अंक दें।"},"4":{"en":"Expel the inactive students from the group immediately without checking if they faced technical or personal barriers.","hi":"यह देखे बिना कि उन्हें तकनीकी या व्यक्तिगत बाधाएँ थीं, निष्क्रिय विद्यार्थियों को तुरंत समूह से बाहर कर दें।"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The teacher has to find the reason behind unequal contribution, so an open and supportive discussion about task allocation comes first<br>It resolves the conflict collaboratively and keeps every student's dignity intact<br>Humiliation, silence or expulsion either harm the students or hide the real problem<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Facilitate a supportive discussion with the entire group to review task allocation and discover why contribution levels are unequal.</b>","hi":"शिक्षक को असमान योगदान का कारण खोजना है, अतः कार्य-विभाजन पर खुली और सहायक चर्चा पहला कदम है<br>यह विवाद को सहयोगपूर्वक सुलझाती है और प्रत्येक विद्यार्थी की गरिमा बनाए रखती है<br>अपमान, चुप्पी या बाहर करना या तो विद्यार्थियों को हानि पहुँचाता है या वास्तविक समस्या छिपा देता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): पूरे समूह के साथ सहायक चर्चा कराएँ जिसमें कार्य-विभाजन की समीक्षा हो और यह पता चले कि योगदान का स्तर असमान क्यों है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000074195","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"In the following question, one statement is given, followed by certain inferences. Consider the statement to be true even if it seems to contradict commonly known facts. Read the inferences carefully and decide which of them logically follow from the given statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>In recent months, sales figures for Panasonic television sets have increased noticeably across various urban and semi-urban markets. The company has reported a steady rise in demand due to improved features and competitive pricing.<br><b>Inferences:</b><br>I. The increase in Panasonic's television sales has led to a corresponding decrease in the sales of television sets of other companies.<br>II. Earlier, Panasonic did not sell any television sets in the market. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में एक कथन और उसके बाद कुछ अनुमान दिए गए हैं। कथन को सत्य मानिए, भले ही वह सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों के विपरीत प्रतीत हो। अनुमानों को ध्यान से पढ़िए और निर्णय कीजिए कि उनमें से कौन-से तार्किक रूप से कथन से निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>हाल के महीनों में विभिन्न शहरी और अर्ध-शहरी बाज़ारों में पैनासोनिक टेलीविज़न सेटों की बिक्री उल्लेखनीय रूप से बढ़ी है। कंपनी ने बेहतर विशेषताओं और प्रतिस्पर्धी मूल्य के कारण माँग में लगातार वृद्धि बताई है।<br><b>अनुमान:</b><br>I. पैनासोनिक की टेलीविज़न बिक्री बढ़ने से अन्य कंपनियों के टेलीविज़न सेटों की बिक्री में समान कमी आई है।<br>II. पहले पैनासोनिक बाज़ार में कोई टेलीविज़न सेट नहीं बेचती थी। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Inference I follows.","hi":"केवल अनुमान I निकलता है।"},"2":{"en":"Only Inference II follows.","hi":"केवल अनुमान II निकलता है।"},"3":{"en":"Both Inferences I and II follow.","hi":"अनुमान I और II दोनों निकलते हैं।"},"4":{"en":"Neither Inference I nor Inference II follows.","hi":"न तो अनुमान I और न ही अनुमान II निकलता है।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The statement only reports higher Panasonic sales and says nothing about the sales of other companies, so I does not follow<br>The rise is credited to improved features, which shows that Panasonic was already selling televisions, so II does not follow<br>Hence neither inference follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Neither Inference I nor Inference II follows.</b>","hi":"कथन केवल पैनासोनिक की बढ़ी हुई बिक्री बताता है और अन्य कंपनियों की बिक्री के बारे में कुछ नहीं कहता, अतः I नहीं निकलता<br>वृद्धि का कारण बेहतर विशेषताएँ बताया गया है, जिससे स्पष्ट है कि पैनासोनिक पहले भी टेलीविज़न बेचती थी, अतः II नहीं निकलता<br>इसलिए कोई भी अनुमान नहीं निकलता<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): न तो अनुमान I और न ही अनुमान II निकलता है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000074196","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"Among the four given combinations, one has error. Identify it.<br>(a) Dr. Raghavendra Rao Subramaniam, Flat No. Bc-1108, Prestige Tall Lakeside Habitat, Whitefield, Bengaluru – 560066<br>(b) Dr. Raghavendra Rao Subramaniam, Flat No. Bc-1108, Prestige Tall Lakeside Habitat, Whitefield, Bengaluru – 560066<br>(c) Dr. Raghavendra Rao Subramaniam, Flat No. Bc-1108, Prestige Tall Lakeside Habitat, Whitefield, Bengaluru – 560066<br>(d) Dr. Raghavendra Rao Subramaniam, Flat No. Bc-1108, Prestige Tall Lakeside Habitate, Whitefield, Bengaluru – 560066 [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दिए गए चार संयोजनों में से एक में त्रुटि है। उसे पहचानिए।<br>(a) Dr. Raghavendra Rao Subramaniam, Flat No. Bc-1108, Prestige Tall Lakeside Habitat, Whitefield, Bengaluru – 560066<br>(b) Dr. Raghavendra Rao Subramaniam, Flat No. Bc-1108, Prestige Tall Lakeside Habitat, Whitefield, Bengaluru – 560066<br>(c) Dr. Raghavendra Rao Subramaniam, Flat No. Bc-1108, Prestige Tall Lakeside Habitat, Whitefield, Bengaluru – 560066<br>(d) Dr. Raghavendra Rao Subramaniam, Flat No. Bc-1108, Prestige Tall Lakeside Habitate, Whitefield, Bengaluru – 560066 [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"a"},"2":{"en":"b"},"3":{"en":"c"},"4":{"en":"d"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Combinations (a), (b) and (c) are exactly the same<br>In (d) the word “Habitat” is written as “Habitate”<br>Hence (d) contains the error<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): d.</b>","hi":"संयोजन (a), (b) और (c) पूर्णतः समान हैं<br>(d) में “Habitat” को “Habitate” लिखा गया है<br>अतः (d) में त्रुटि है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): d है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000074197","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"A project manager notices a growing interpersonal conflict between two key team members during a high-stakes project. One member is visibly frustrated and vocal, while the other has completely shut down and is withdrawing from team discussions.<br>Which response by the project manager demonstrates the highest emotional intelligence (EI)? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक परियोजना प्रबंधक को एक महत्वपूर्ण परियोजना के दौरान दो प्रमुख टीम सदस्यों के बीच बढ़ते पारस्परिक टकराव का पता चलता है। एक सदस्य स्पष्ट रूप से नाराज़ और मुखर है, जबकि दूसरा पूरी तरह चुप हो गया है और टीम चर्चाओं से कट रहा है।<br>परियोजना प्रबंधक की कौन-सी प्रतिक्रिया सर्वाधिक भावनात्मक बुद्धिमत्ता (EI) दर्शाती है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ignore the tension entirely to let them naturally resolve the issue on their own.","hi":"तनाव को पूरी तरह अनदेखा करें ताकि वे स्वयं मामला सुलझा लें।"},"2":{"en":"Reassign one team member immediately to eliminate the discomfort of workplace friction.","hi":"कार्यस्थल के टकराव की असुविधा हटाने के लिए तुरंत एक सदस्य को दूसरी जगह नियुक्त कर दें।"},"3":{"en":"Schedule private, separate one-on-one meetings to understand both perspectives before facilitating a resolution.","hi":"समाधान सुगम बनाने से पहले दोनों दृष्टिकोण समझने के लिए अलग-अलग निजी बैठकें करें।"},"4":{"en":"Publicly side with the vocal team member because their frustration indicates higher engagement.","hi":"सार्वजनिक रूप से मुखर सदस्य का पक्ष लें क्योंकि उसकी नाराज़गी अधिक जुड़ाव दर्शाती है।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Emotional intelligence means understanding both sides before acting, so separate one-on-one meetings gather the full picture privately<br>Only after hearing both members can a fair and lasting resolution be facilitated<br>Ignoring the conflict, shifting a member or taking sides all leave the real problem unresolved<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Schedule private, separate one-on-one meetings to understand both perspectives before facilitating a resolution.</b>","hi":"भावनात्मक बुद्धिमत्ता का अर्थ कार्य करने से पहले दोनों पक्षों को समझना है, अतः अलग-अलग निजी बैठकों में पूरी जानकारी मिलती है<br>दोनों सदस्यों को सुनने के बाद ही निष्पक्ष और स्थायी समाधान सुगम हो सकता है<br>टकराव अनदेखा करना, सदस्य बदलना या पक्ष लेना वास्तविक समस्या को अनसुलझा छोड़ देता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): समाधान सुगम बनाने से पहले दोनों दृष्टिकोण समझने के लिए अलग-अलग निजी बैठकें करें। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000074198","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"Pollution levels are rising, affecting public health and increasing healthcare costs. What would you suggest to the government to mitigate this crisis? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"प्रदूषण का स्तर बढ़ रहा है, जिससे जन-स्वास्थ्य प्रभावित हो रहा है और स्वास्थ्य सेवा लागत बढ़ रही है। इस संकट को कम करने के लिए आप सरकार को क्या सुझाव देंगे? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Increase taxes on industrial units.","hi":"औद्योगिक इकाइयों पर कर बढ़ाए जाएँ।"},"2":{"en":"Adopt green energy technology solutions.","hi":"हरित ऊर्जा प्रौद्योगिकी समाधान अपनाए जाएँ।"},"3":{"en":"Ban all private vehicle usage.","hi":"सभी निजी वाहनों के उपयोग पर प्रतिबंध लगाया जाए।"},"4":{"en":"Construct many more urban clinics.","hi":"बहुत अधिक शहरी क्लिनिक बनाए जाएँ।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The crisis is caused by rising pollution, so the remedy must attack the source of pollution itself<br>Switching to green energy technology reduces emissions at the source and improves health in the long run<br>Higher taxes, a complete vehicle ban or more clinics only treat symptoms or create new hardship<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Adopt green energy technology solutions.</b>","hi":"संकट बढ़ते प्रदूषण के कारण है, अतः उपाय प्रदूषण के स्रोत पर ही प्रहार करना चाहिए<br>हरित ऊर्जा प्रौद्योगिकी अपनाने से उत्सर्जन स्रोत पर ही घटता है और दीर्घकाल में स्वास्थ्य सुधरता है<br>अधिक कर, वाहनों पर पूर्ण प्रतिबंध या अधिक क्लिनिक केवल लक्षणों का उपचार करते हैं या नई कठिनाई पैदा करते हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): हरित ऊर्जा प्रौद्योगिकी समाधान अपनाए जाएँ। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000074199","section":"REASONING","topic":"Matrix","question":{"en":"Which of the following rows/columns are connected/related with each other in some way?<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td rowspan=\"2\" style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Rows</td><td colspan=\"5\" style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px;text-align:center\">Columns</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">I</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">II</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">III</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">IV</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">V</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">1</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">27</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">64</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">16</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">13</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">125</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">25</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">15</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">216</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">11</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">36</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">16</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">343</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">13</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">49</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">18</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी पंक्तियाँ/स्तंभ किसी प्रकार एक-दूसरे से जुड़े/संबंधित हैं?<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td rowspan=\"2\" style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Rows</td><td colspan=\"5\" style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px;text-align:center\">Columns</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">I</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">II</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">III</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">IV</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">V</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">1</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">27</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">64</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">16</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">13</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">125</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">25</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">15</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">216</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">11</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">36</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">16</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">343</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">13</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">49</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">18</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Columns I, III and V","hi":"स्तंभ I, III और V"},"2":{"en":"Columns I, III and IV","hi":"स्तंभ I, III और IV"},"3":{"en":"Columns I, II and IV","hi":"स्तंभ I, II और IV"},"4":{"en":"Columns I, IV and V","hi":"स्तंभ I, IV और V"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Column II is the cube of column I (3³ = 27, 4³ = 64, 5³ = 125) and column IV is the square of column I (3² = 9, 4² = 16, 5² = 25)<br>So columns I, II and IV move together in a fixed relation in every row<br>Hence columns I, II and IV are the connected ones<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Columns I, II and IV.</b>","hi":"स्तंभ II, स्तंभ I का घन है (3³ = 27, 4³ = 64, 5³ = 125) और स्तंभ IV, स्तंभ I का वर्ग है (3² = 9, 4² = 16, 5² = 25)<br>अतः प्रत्येक पंक्ति में स्तंभ I, II और IV एक निश्चित संबंध में साथ चलते हैं<br>इसलिए स्तंभ I, II और IV परस्पर जुड़े हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): स्तंभ I, II और IV है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000074200","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"FROZEN\" is written as \"FsOaEo\". How will \"MARKET\" be written in the same code language? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"किसी निश्चित कूट भाषा में \"FROZEN\" को \"FsOaEo\" लिखा जाता है। उसी कूट भाषा में \"MARKET\" को कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"MbRlEv"},"2":{"en":"MbRlFu"},"3":{"en":"MbRkEu"},"4":{"en":"MbRlEu"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Odd-placed letters stay the same and even-placed letters move one step forward as small letters: F R O Z E N → F s O a E o (R→s, Z→a as the alphabet starts again, N→o)<br>MARKET: M, A→b, R, K→l, E, T→u<br>Code = MbRlEu<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): MbRlEu.</b>","hi":"विषम स्थान के अक्षर वैसे ही रहते हैं और सम स्थान के अक्षर एक कदम आगे छोटे अक्षरों में आते हैं: F R O Z E N → F s O a E o (R→s, Z के बाद वर्णमाला फिर आरम्भ होती है अतः Z→a, N→o)<br>MARKET: M, A→b, R, K→l, E, T→u<br>कूट = MbRlEu<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): MbRlEu है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000074201","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"FINGER\" is written as \"FjNhEs\". How will \"GARDEN\" be written in the same code language? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"किसी निश्चित कूट भाषा में \"FINGER\" को \"FjNhEs\" लिखा जाता है। उसी कूट भाषा में \"GARDEN\" को कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"GbReFo"},"2":{"en":"GbReEo"},"3":{"en":"GbRdEo"},"4":{"en":"GcReEo"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Odd-placed letters stay the same and even-placed letters move one place ahead as small letters: F I N G E R → F j N h E s<br>GARDEN gives G b R e E o<br>Code = GbReEo<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): GbReEo.</b>","hi":"विषम स्थान के अक्षर वैसे ही रहते हैं और सम स्थान के अक्षर एक स्थान आगे छोटे अक्षरों में बदलते हैं: F I N G E R → F j N h E s<br>GARDEN से G b R e E o<br>कूट = GbReEo<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): GbReEo है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000074202","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Course of Action","question":{"en":"Direction:<br>Select the best course of action.<br>A company has a limited budget and must choose between upgrading cybersecurity systems or expanding customer service operations. Internal reports indicate moderate cybersecurity risks and growing customer complaints. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निर्देश:<br>सर्वोत्तम कार्यवाही चुनिए।<br>एक कंपनी का बजट सीमित है और उसे साइबर सुरक्षा प्रणालियों के उन्नयन तथा ग्राहक सेवा संचालन के विस्तार में से एक चुनना है। आंतरिक रिपोर्ट मध्यम साइबर सुरक्षा जोखिम तथा बढ़ती ग्राहक शिकायतें दर्शाती हैं। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Allocate all resources to customer service because complaints are immediately visible.","hi":"सभी संसाधन ग्राहक सेवा को दें क्योंकि शिकायतें तुरंत दिखाई देती हैं।"},"2":{"en":"Allocate all resources to cybersecurity because security risks can become severe.","hi":"सभी संसाधन साइबर सुरक्षा को दें क्योंकि सुरक्षा जोखिम गंभीर हो सकते हैं।"},"3":{"en":"Assess the relative impact of both risks and distribute resources according to priority.","hi":"दोनों जोखिमों के सापेक्ष प्रभाव का आकलन करें और प्राथमिकता के अनुसार संसाधन बाँटें।"},"4":{"en":"Delay both initiatives until a larger budget becomes available.","hi":"बड़ा बजट उपलब्ध होने तक दोनों पहलों को टाल दें।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Both areas carry real risk, so spending everything on one of them leaves the other unprotected<br>Comparing the impact of the two risks and dividing the limited budget by priority handles both dangers sensibly<br>Postponing everything increases both the security risk and the customer dissatisfaction<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Assess the relative impact of both risks and distribute resources according to priority.</b>","hi":"दोनों क्षेत्रों में वास्तविक जोखिम है, अतः सब कुछ एक पर खर्च करने से दूसरा असुरक्षित रह जाता है<br>दोनों जोखिमों के प्रभाव की तुलना करके सीमित बजट प्राथमिकता से बाँटना दोनों खतरों को समझदारी से संभालता है<br>सब कुछ टालने से सुरक्षा जोखिम तथा ग्राहक असंतोष दोनों बढ़ते हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): दोनों जोखिमों के सापेक्ष प्रभाव का आकलन करें और प्राथमिकता के अनुसार संसाधन बाँटें। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000074203","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Study the pattern in the given series and find the next set of letters in the series.<br>MOM, JSJ, GWG, DAD, ? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दी गई श्रेणी का पैटर्न अध्ययन कीजिए और अक्षरों का अगला समूह ज्ञात कीजिए।<br>MOM, JSJ, GWG, DAD, ? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"AEA"},"2":{"en":"GDA"},"3":{"en":"CBC"},"4":{"en":"ACA"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"First letters M, J, G, D go 3 back each time, so next is A<br>Second letters O, S, W, A go 4 forward, so next is E<br>Third letters M, J, G, D also go 3 back, so next is A<br>Next group = AEA<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): AEA.</b>","hi":"पहले अक्षर M, J, G, D हर बार 3 पीछे, अतः अगला A<br>दूसरे अक्षर O, S, W, A हर बार 4 आगे, अतः अगला E<br>तीसरे अक्षर M, J, G, D भी हर बार 3 पीछे, अतः अगला A<br>अगला समूह = AEA<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): AEA है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000074204","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"Read the given statement carefully and the following assumptions based on it. Decide which of the assumptions are implicit in the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>To alleviate the severe shortage of parking spaces in the city centre, the municipal corporation plans to impose a heavy 'congestion surcharge' on all private vehicles entering the downtown area during peak hours.<br><b>Assumptions:</b><br>I. The current parking shortage is primarily driven by the excessive volume of private vehicles commuting to the city centre, rather than a lack of parking infrastructure.<br>II. A significant percentage of commuters will choose alternative modes of transport or adjust their travel times to avoid paying the additional congestion surcharge. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दिया गया कथन ध्यान से पढ़िए और उस पर आधारित अनुमानों को देखिए। निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-से अनुमान कथन में निहित हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>शहर के केंद्र में पार्किंग स्थानों की गंभीर कमी को कम करने के लिए नगर निगम व्यस्त समय में डाउनटाउन क्षेत्र में प्रवेश करने वाले सभी निजी वाहनों पर भारी 'भीड़-भाड़ अधिभार' लगाने की योजना बना रहा है।<br><b>अनुमान:</b><br>I. वर्तमान पार्किंग की कमी मुख्य रूप से शहर के केंद्र में आने वाले निजी वाहनों की अत्यधिक संख्या के कारण है, न कि पार्किंग अवसंरचना की कमी के कारण।<br>II. महत्वपूर्ण प्रतिशत यात्री अतिरिक्त भीड़-भाड़ अधिभार से बचने के लिए वैकल्पिक परिवहन साधन चुनेंगे या अपने यात्रा समय में बदलाव करेंगे। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Assumption II is implicit","hi":"केवल अनुमान II निहित है"},"2":{"en":"Neither Assumption I nor II is implicit","hi":"न तो अनुमान I और न ही II निहित है"},"3":{"en":"Both Assumptions I and II are implicit","hi":"अनुमान I और II दोनों निहित हैं"},"4":{"en":"Only Assumption I is implicit","hi":"केवल अनुमान I निहित है"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Charging vehicles is a sensible remedy only if the vehicles themselves, and not the lack of parking space, cause the shortage, so I is implicit<br>The surcharge can work only if a sizeable number of commuters change their transport or timing, so II is implicit<br>Hence both assumptions are implicit<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Both Assumptions I and II are implicit.</b>","hi":"वाहनों पर शुल्क लगाना तभी उपयुक्त उपाय है जब कमी वाहनों के कारण हो, पार्किंग स्थान की कमी के कारण न हो, अतः I निहित है<br>अधिभार तभी काम कर सकता है जब पर्याप्त संख्या में यात्री अपना साधन या समय बदलें, अतः II निहित है<br>इसलिए दोनों अनुमान निहित हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): अनुमान I और II दोनों निहित हैं है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000074205","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Analogy","question":{"en":"Select the option that is related to the third word in the same way as the second word is related to the first word. (The words must be considered as meaningful English words and must not be related to each other based on the number of letters/number of consonants/vowels in the word.)<br>Anemometer : Wind Speed :: Seismograph : ? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"उस विकल्प का चयन कीजिए जो तीसरे शब्द से उसी प्रकार संबंधित है जिस प्रकार दूसरा शब्द पहले शब्द से संबंधित है। (शब्दों को अर्थपूर्ण अंग्रेज़ी शब्द मानना है और उन्हें अक्षरों/व्यंजनों/स्वरों की संख्या के आधार पर एक-दूसरे से संबंधित नहीं मानना है।)<br>Anemometer : Wind Speed :: Seismograph : ? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Earthquake Vibrations","hi":"भूकंपीय कंपन"},"2":{"en":"Rainfall","hi":"वर्षा"},"3":{"en":"Ocean Currents","hi":"महासागरीय धाराएँ"},"4":{"en":"Air Pressure","hi":"वायु दाब"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"An anemometer is an instrument used to measure wind speed<br>A seismograph is an instrument used to record earthquake vibrations<br>So the answer is earthquake vibrations<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Earthquake Vibrations.</b>","hi":"एनीमोमीटर वायु की गति मापने का यंत्र है<br>सीस्मोग्राफ भूकंपीय कंपन दर्ज करने का यंत्र है<br>अतः उत्तर भूकंपीय कंपन है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): भूकंपीय कंपन है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000074206","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Budget and Taxation","question":{"en":"Which of the following ministries prepared the budget in India? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारत में बजट निम्नलिखित में से किस मंत्रालय द्वारा तैयार किया जाता है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Commerce and Industry","hi":"वाणिज्य एवं उद्योग"},"2":{"en":"Finance","hi":"वित्त"},"3":{"en":"Planning","hi":"योजना"},"4":{"en":"Corporate affairs","hi":"कॉर्पोरेट कार्य"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Finance</b><br>The Union Budget is prepared by the <b>Budget Division of the Department of Economic Affairs</b>, which works under the <b>Ministry of Finance</b>, and it is presented in Parliament by the <b>Finance Minister</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Budget is laid before Parliament as the <b>Annual Financial Statement</b> under <b>Article 112</b>, and it is presented on <b>1 February</b> for the financial year beginning 1 April.<br>• Since 2017 the <b>Railway Budget</b> is merged with the Union Budget, and the plan and non-plan classification of expenditure was replaced by the revenue and capital classification.<br>• The <b>Ministry of Commerce and Industry</b> handles trade and industrial policy, while the <b>Ministry of Corporate Affairs</b> administers the Companies Act, 2013.<br>• The <b>Planning Commission</b> never prepared the Budget; it was replaced by <b>NITI Aayog</b> in 2015.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – वित्त</b><br>केंद्रीय बजट <b>वित्त मंत्रालय</b> के अधीनस्थ <b>आर्थिक कार्य विभाग के बजट प्रभाग</b> द्वारा तैयार किया जाता है और इसे <b>वित्त मंत्री</b> संसद में प्रस्तुत करते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• बजट संसद के समक्ष <b>अनुच्छेद 112</b> के अंतर्गत <b>वार्षिक वित्तीय विवरण</b> के रूप में रखा जाता है तथा 1 अप्रैल से प्रारंभ होने वाले वित्त वर्ष हेतु <b>1 फरवरी</b> को प्रस्तुत होता है।<br>• वर्ष 2017 से <b>रेल बजट</b> केंद्रीय बजट में विलीन कर दिया गया तथा योजना व गैर-योजना व्यय के स्थान पर राजस्व व पूँजीगत वर्गीकरण लागू हुआ।<br>• <b>वाणिज्य एवं उद्योग मंत्रालय</b> व्यापार व औद्योगिक नीति देखता है, जबकि <b>कॉर्पोरेट कार्य मंत्रालय</b> कंपनी अधिनियम, 2013 का प्रशासन करता है।<br>• <b>योजना आयोग</b> ने कभी बजट तैयार नहीं किया; 2015 में इसके स्थान पर <b>नीति आयोग</b> बनाया गया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000074207","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Monetary Policy","question":{"en":"In money supply, M3 refers to which of the following? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"मुद्रा आपूर्ति में M3 निम्नलिखित में से किसे संदर्भित करता है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"M1 + savings deposits with post office savings banks","hi":"M1 + डाकघर बचत बैंकों की बचत जमा"},"2":{"en":"M1 - savings deposits with post office savings banks","hi":"M1 - डाकघर बचत बैंकों की बचत जमा"},"3":{"en":"M1 + net time deposits of banks","hi":"M1 + बैंकों की शुद्ध सावधि जमा"},"4":{"en":"M1 - net time deposits of banks","hi":"M1 - बैंकों की शुद्ध सावधि जमा"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – M1 + net time deposits of banks</b><br><b>M3</b> (broad money) is defined as <b>M1 plus net time deposits with banks</b>. It is the most widely used measure of money supply in India and is also called aggregate monetary resources.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>M1</b> = currency with the public + demand deposits with banks + other deposits with the RBI; it is the most liquid measure, called narrow money.<br>• <b>M2</b> = M1 + savings deposits with post office savings banks.<br>• <b>M4</b> = M3 + total deposits with the post office savings organisation, excluding National Savings Certificates.<br>• Liquidity decreases from M1 to M4, while the value of the aggregate increases; the RBI publishes all four measures in its monetary survey.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – M1 + बैंकों की शुद्ध सावधि जमा</b><br><b>M3</b> (व्यापक मुद्रा) को <b>M1 तथा बैंकों की शुद्ध सावधि जमा के योग</b> के रूप में परिभाषित किया जाता है। भारत में मुद्रा आपूर्ति का यह सर्वाधिक प्रयुक्त मापदंड है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>M1</b> = जनता के पास मुद्रा + बैंकों की माँग जमा + RBI के पास अन्य जमा; यह सर्वाधिक तरल माप है, जिसे संकीर्ण मुद्रा कहते हैं।<br>• <b>M2</b> = M1 + डाकघर बचत बैंकों की बचत जमा।<br>• <b>M4</b> = M3 + राष्ट्रीय बचत प्रमाणपत्रों को छोड़कर डाकघर बचत संगठन की कुल जमा।<br>• M1 से M4 की ओर तरलता घटती जाती है, जबकि कुल राशि का मान बढ़ता जाता है; RBI अपनी मौद्रिक समीक्षा में चारों माप प्रकाशित करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000074208","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: International News","question":{"en":"What is a key element of the IMEC (India-Middle East-Europe Economic Corridor) infrastructure? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"IMEC (भारत-मध्य पूर्व-यूरोप आर्थिक कॉरिडोर) की अवसंरचना का प्रमुख तत्व क्या है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Space elevators","hi":"अंतरिक्ष लिफ्ट"},"2":{"en":"Pipelines","hi":"पाइपलाइन"},"3":{"en":"Zeppelin routes","hi":"ज़ेपेलिन मार्ग"},"4":{"en":"Underground hyperloops","hi":"भूमिगत हाइपरलूप"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Pipelines</b><br>The <b>India-Middle East-Europe Economic Corridor (IMEC)</b> is a multi-modal corridor that combines a <b>railway network</b> with <b>electricity cables, a hydrogen pipeline and a data cable</b>, besides shipping links. <b>Pipelines</b> for clean hydrogen and energy therefore form a core part of its infrastructure.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The IMEC was announced through a Memorandum of Understanding signed on the sidelines of the <b>G20 Summit in New Delhi in September 2023</b>.<br>• The signatories include <b>India, the United States, Saudi Arabia, the United Arab Emirates, the European Union, France, Germany and Italy</b>.<br>• The corridor is to connect India with the Gulf and then Europe through <b>rail and shipping routes</b>, cutting transit time and logistics cost for trade.<br>• It is projected as a greener, shorter alternative that complements existing routes such as the <b>Suez Canal</b> and the International North-South Transport Corridor.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – पाइपलाइन</b><br><b>भारत-मध्य पूर्व-यूरोप आर्थिक कॉरिडोर (IMEC)</b> एक बहु-मॉडल कॉरिडोर है जिसमें <b>रेल नेटवर्क</b> के साथ <b>बिजली केबल, हाइड्रोजन पाइपलाइन तथा डेटा केबल</b> और समुद्री मार्ग सम्मिलित हैं। इसलिए स्वच्छ ऊर्जा हेतु <b>पाइपलाइन</b> इसकी अवसंरचना का मूल तत्व है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• IMEC की घोषणा <b>सितंबर 2023</b> में <b>नई दिल्ली में आयोजित G20 शिखर सम्मेलन</b> के अवसर पर हस्ताक्षरित समझौता ज्ञापन के माध्यम से की गई थी।<br>• इस पर हस्ताक्षर करने वालों में <b>भारत, अमेरिका, सऊदी अरब, संयुक्त अरब अमीरात, यूरोपीय संघ, फ्रांस, जर्मनी व इटली</b> सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• यह कॉरिडोर भारत को खाड़ी देशों तथा वहाँ से यूरोप से <b>रेल व समुद्री मार्गों</b> से जोड़कर व्यापार का पारगमन समय व लागत घटाएगा।<br>• इसे <b>स्वेज नहर</b> तथा अंतर्राष्ट्रीय उत्तर-दक्षिण परिवहन कॉरिडोर जैसे वर्तमान मार्गों का पूरक और अधिक हरा-भरा विकल्प बताया गया है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000074209","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"How many players are on a standard team in a game of Ultimate Frisbee? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"अल्टीमेट फ्रिस्बी के खेल में एक मानक टीम में कितने खिलाड़ी होते हैं? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5"},"2":{"en":"6"},"3":{"en":"7"},"4":{"en":"8"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 7</b><br>In <b>Ultimate Frisbee</b>, each team fields <b>seven players</b> at a time on a regulation outdoor field. The sport is played with a flying disc and the object is to pass the disc into the opposing end zone.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The sport is governed internationally by the <b>World Flying Disc Federation (WFDF)</b>, and its flying disc weighs <b>175 grams</b>.<br>• A regulation field is about <b>110 metres long and 37 metres wide</b>, including end zones of 18 metres each.<br>• Ultimate is self-refereed and is famous for the <b>Spirit of the Game</b>, under which players themselves call fouls.<br>• Indoor Ultimate is played with <b>five players</b> a side, which is why 5 is the closest wrong option here.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 7</b><br><b>अल्टीमेट फ्रिस्बी</b> में प्रत्येक टीम मानक बाहरी मैदान पर एक समय में <b>सात खिलाड़ी</b> उतारती है। यह खेल उड़ने वाली डिस्क से खेला जाता है और इसका उद्देश्य डिस्क को विरोधी पक्ष के एंड ज़ोन में पहुँचाना है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इस खेल का अंतर्राष्ट्रीय नियामक <b>विश्व फ्लाइंग डिस्क महासंघ (WFDF)</b> है, तथा इसकी डिस्क का भार <b>175 ग्राम</b> होता है।<br>• मानक मैदान लगभग <b>110 मीटर लंबा व 37 मीटर चौड़ा</b> होता है, जिसमें 18 मीटर के दो एंड ज़ोन सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• अल्टीमेट स्वनिर्णायक खेल है और यह <b>खेल की भावना (Spirit of the Game)</b> के लिए प्रसिद्ध है, जिसमें फाउल की घोषणा स्वयं खिलाड़ी करते हैं।<br>• इनडोर अल्टीमेट में प्रत्येक पक्ष के <b>पाँच खिलाड़ी</b> होते हैं, इसीलिए यहाँ 5 निकटतम गलत विकल्प है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000074210","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"In which Indian city did the <b>2016</b> South Asian Games' table tennis events primarily take place? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"<b>2016</b> के दक्षिण एशियाई खेलों की टेबल टेनिस स्पर्धाएँ मुख्य रूप से भारत के किस शहर में हुई थीं? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Bhopal","hi":"भोपाल"},"2":{"en":"Guwahati","hi":"गुवाहाटी"},"3":{"en":"Imphal","hi":"इम्फाल"},"4":{"en":"Aizawl","hi":"आइजोल"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Guwahati</b><br>The <b>12th South Asian Games in 2016</b> were jointly hosted by <b>Guwahati and Shillong</b>, and the table tennis events were held at the indoor stadium in <b>Guwahati</b>, Assam.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The 2016 Games were the <b>12th edition</b> of the South Asian Games and were held in <b>February 2016</b>.<br>• India topped the medal tally, followed by Sri Lanka and Pakistan.<br>• The mascot of the 2016 Games was <b>Tikhor</b>, the one-horned rhinoceros.<br>• These were the third South Asian Games hosted by India after <b>Kolkata 1987 and Chennai 1995</b>, and their official theme was the Games of the <b>Eight North Eastern States</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – गुवाहाटी</b><br><b>2016 के 12वें दक्षिण एशियाई खेलों</b> की सह-मेज़बानी <b>गुवाहाटी तथा शिलांग</b> ने की, और टेबल टेनिस स्पर्धाएँ असम के <b>गुवाहाटी</b> स्थित इनडोर स्टेडियम में हुईं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• 2016 के खेल दक्षिण एशियाई खेलों का <b>12वाँ संस्करण</b> थे और <b>फरवरी 2016</b> में आयोजित हुए।<br>• पदक तालिका में भारत शीर्ष पर रहा, उसके बाद श्रीलंका तथा पाकिस्तान रहे।<br>• 2016 के खेलों का शुभंकर <b>टिखोर</b> था, जो एक सींग वाला गैंडा है।<br>• भारत द्वारा आयोजित ये तीसरे दक्षिण एशियाई खेल थे - इससे पूर्व <b>कोलकाता 1987 व चेन्नई 1995</b> में हुए थे।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000074211","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Which organization, abbreviated as NADA, is responsible for monitoring and ensuring fair play in sports through anti-doping measures in India? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारत में डोप-विरोधी उपायों के माध्यम से खेलों में निष्पक्षता की निगरानी और सुनिश्चितता हेतु NADA संक्षिप्त नाम वाला कौन-सा संगठन उत्तरदायी है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"National Athletic Drug Agency","hi":"राष्ट्रीय एथलेटिक औषधि एजेंसी"},"2":{"en":"National Anti-Doping Agency","hi":"राष्ट्रीय डोप-विरोधी एजेंसी"},"3":{"en":"National Association of Drug Analysis","hi":"राष्ट्रीय औषधि विश्लेषण संघ"},"4":{"en":"National Athlete Development Authority","hi":"राष्ट्रीय खिलाड़ी विकास प्राधिकरण"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – National Anti-Doping Agency</b><br><b>NADA</b> stands for the <b>National Anti-Doping Agency</b>, an autonomous body under the <b>Ministry of Youth Affairs and Sports</b> that plans, coordinates and monitors dope testing in Indian sports.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• NADA was set up in <b>2005</b> with its headquarters at <b>New Delhi</b> and became a signatory to the <b>World Anti-Doping Code</b> of WADA.<br>• Sample analysis is done by the <b>National Dope Testing Laboratory (NDTL)</b>, New Delhi, which is accredited by the World Anti-Doping Agency.<br>• NADA runs the <b>National Anti-Doping Programme</b>, including in-competition and out-of-competition testing of athletes.<br>• A positive test can lead to sanctions such as a <b>four-year ban</b> and disqualification of results under the WADA Code.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – राष्ट्रीय डोप-विरोधी एजेंसी</b><br><b>NADA</b> का पूर्ण रूप <b>राष्ट्रीय डोप-विरोधी एजेंसी (National Anti-Doping Agency)</b> है, जो <b>युवा कार्यक्रम एवं खेल मंत्रालय</b> के अधीन एक स्वायत्त निकाय है और भारतीय खेलों में डोप परीक्षण की योजना, समन्वय व निगरानी करता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• NADA की स्थापना <b>2005</b> में हुई और इसका मुख्यालय <b>नई दिल्ली</b> में है; यह WADA की <b>विश्व डोप-विरोधी संहिता</b> का हस्ताक्षरकर्ता है।<br>• नमूनों का विश्लेषण <b>राष्ट्रीय डोप परीक्षण प्रयोगशाला (NDTL)</b>, नई दिल्ली में होता है, जो विश्व डोप-विरोधी एजेंसी से मान्यता प्राप्त है।<br>• NADA <b>राष्ट्रीय डोप-विरोधी कार्यक्रम</b> चलाता है, जिसमें प्रतियोगिता के दौरान तथा बाहर दोनों प्रकार के परीक्षण सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• सकारात्मक परीक्षण पर <b>चार वर्ष तक का प्रतिबंध</b> तथा परिणामों का निरस्तीकरण जैसे दंड लगाए जा सकते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000074212","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: President and Vice President of India","question":{"en":"Who is the 15th President of India? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारत के 15वें राष्ट्रपति कौन हैं? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Droupadi Murmu","hi":"द्रौपदी मुर्मू"},"2":{"en":"Pranab Mukherjee","hi":"प्रणब मुखर्जी"},"3":{"en":"Ram Nath Kovind","hi":"रामनाथ कोविंद"},"4":{"en":"Pratibha Patil","hi":"प्रतिभा पाटिल"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Droupadi Murmu</b><br><b>Droupadi Murmu</b> is the <b>15th President of India</b>. She took the oath of office on <b>25 July 2022</b> and is the first tribal woman and the second woman to hold the office.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• She was the <b>Governor of Jharkhand</b> before becoming President and belongs to the Santhal tribal community of Odisha.<br>• The President is elected by an <b>electoral college</b> under <b>Article 54</b>, and the term of office is five years under Article 56.<br>• <b>Pratibha Patil</b> was the 12th and first woman President, <b>Pranab Mukherjee</b> the 13th and <b>Ram Nath Kovind</b> the 14th, who held office from 2017 to 2022.<br>• The President is the <b>supreme commander of the armed forces</b> and exercises executive power on the advice of the Council of Ministers under Article 53.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – द्रौपदी मुर्मू</b><br><b>द्रौपदी मुर्मू</b> भारत की <b>15वीं राष्ट्रपति</b> हैं। उन्होंने <b>25 जुलाई 2022</b> को पद की शपथ ली और वे इस पद पर पहुँचने वाली पहली जनजातीय महिला तथा दूसरी महिला हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• राष्ट्रपति बनने से पूर्व वे <b>झारखंड की राज्यपाल</b> थीं और ओडिशा की संथाल जनजाति से संबंधित हैं।<br>• राष्ट्रपति का चुनाव <b>अनुच्छेद 54</b> के अंतर्गत <b>निर्वाचक मंडल</b> द्वारा होता है तथा अनुच्छेद 56 के अनुसार कार्यकाल पाँच वर्ष का होता है।<br>• <b>प्रतिभा पाटिल</b> 12वीं तथा प्रथम महिला राष्ट्रपति थीं, <b>प्रणब मुखर्जी</b> 13वें तथा <b>रामनाथ कोविंद</b> 14वें राष्ट्रपति थे, जो 2017 से 2022 तक पद पर रहे।<br>• राष्ट्रपति <b>सशस्त्र बलों के सर्वोच्च कमांडर</b> होते हैं और अनुच्छेद 53 के अनुसार मंत्रिपरिषद की सलाह पर कार्यपालिका शक्ति का प्रयोग करते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000074213","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Jainism and Buddhism","question":{"en":"Which among the following is NOT a feature of a stupa? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा स्तूप की विशेषता नहीं है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Harmika","hi":"हार्मिका"},"2":{"en":"Artha Mandapa","hi":"अर्थ मंडप"},"3":{"en":"Pradakshina Patha","hi":"प्रदक्षिणा पथ"},"4":{"en":"Torana","hi":"तोरण"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Artha Mandapa</b><br>A stupa consists of the <b>Anda</b> (dome), <b>Harmika</b> (railing on top), <b>Chattra</b> (umbrella), <b>Medhi</b> (platform), <b>Pradakshina Patha</b> (circumambulatory passage) and <b>Torana</b> (gateways). The <b>Artha Mandapa</b> is the assembly hall of a Hindu temple, not part of a stupa.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The stupa evolved from a simple <b>burial mound</b> containing relics of the Buddha and became the most characteristic form of Buddhist architecture.<br>• <b>Sanchi Stupa</b> in Madhya Pradesh, built by Ashoka in the 3rd century BCE, is the oldest surviving stone stupa and has four richly carved toranas.<br>• The <b>Pradakshina Patha</b> allowed devotees to walk around the sacred dome in a clockwise direction.<br>• In temple architecture, the <b>Artha Mandapa</b> precedes the main shrine and is used for dances and rituals.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – अर्थ मंडप</b><br>स्तूप में <b>अंड</b> (गुंबद), <b>हार्मिका</b> (शीर्ष की रेलिंग), <b>छत्र</b> (छत्राकार), <b>मेधि</b> (चबूतरा), <b>प्रदक्षिणा पथ</b> तथा <b>तोरण</b> (प्रवेश द्वार) होते हैं। <b>अर्थ मंडप</b> हिंदू मंदिर का सभा कक्ष है, स्तूप का अंग नहीं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• स्तूप का विकास बुद्ध के अवशेषों पर बने <b>समाधि-टीले</b> से हुआ और यह बौद्ध स्थापत्य का सर्वाधिक विशिष्ट रूप बना।<br>• मध्य प्रदेश का <b>साँची स्तूप</b>, जिसे अशोक ने तीसरी शताब्दी ईसा पूर्व में बनवाया, प्राचीनतम विद्यमान पाषाण स्तूप है तथा इसके चारों तोरण अलंकृत हैं।<br>• <b>प्रदक्षिणा पथ</b> से श्रद्धालु पवित्र गुंबद के चारों ओर दक्षिणावर्त परिक्रमा करते थे।<br>• मंदिर स्थापत्य में <b>अर्थ मंडप</b> गर्भगृह से पहले आता है और नृत्य व अनुष्ठानों हेतु प्रयुक्त होता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000074214","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Music and Musical Instruments","question":{"en":"Which musical form from the Dhrupad tradition involves a slow improvisational introduction with emphasis on the 'alap,' followed by a rhythmic section with a fixed composition? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"ध्रुपद परंपरा का कौन-सा संगीत रूप 'आलाप' पर बल देते हुए धीमी आलाप-प्रधान प्रस्तुति से आरंभ होकर निश्चित रचना वाले लयबद्ध भाग में परिणत होता है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Thumri","hi":"ठुमरी"},"2":{"en":"Khyal","hi":"ख्याल"},"3":{"en":"Dhrupad","hi":"ध्रुपद"},"4":{"en":"Tappa","hi":"टप्पा"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Dhrupad</b><br><b>Dhrupad</b> is the oldest surviving form of Hindustani classical music. Its performance opens with a slow, unhurried <b>alap</b> in free rhythm, and is followed by a rhythmic section built on a <b>fixed composition</b> set to a <b>tala</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• A Dhrupad composition has four parts: <b>Sthayi, Antara, Sanchari and Abhog</b>, and it is accompanied by the <b>pakhawaj</b>.<br>• The famous <b>Dagar</b> and <b>Gundecha</b> families are its best-known exponents; there are four <b>vanis</b> or styles - Gauhar, Nauhar, Khandar and Dagar.<br>• <b>Khyal</b> is a comparatively free and ornamented form, <b>Thumri</b> belongs to the light classical style, and <b>Tappa</b> is known for its swift, tumbling phrases.<br>• Dhrupad is closely linked with the <b>Mughal court</b>, where Man Singh Tomar and later Tansen composed in this form.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – ध्रुपद</b><br><b>ध्रुपद</b> हिंदुस्तानी शास्त्रीय संगीत का प्राचीनतम प्रचलित रूप है। इसकी प्रस्तुति मुक्त लय में धीमे <b>आलाप</b> से आरंभ होती है और इसके बाद <b>ताल</b> में निबद्ध <b>निश्चित रचना</b> पर आधारित लयबद्ध भाग आता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• ध्रुपद रचना के चार भाग होते हैं - <b>स्थायी, अंतरा, संचारी व आभोग</b>, तथा इसके साथ <b>पखावज</b> बजाया जाता है।<br>• <b>डागर</b> तथा <b>गुंडेचा</b> परिवार इसके प्रसिद्ध कलाकार हैं; इसकी चार <b>वाणियाँ</b> हैं - गौहर, नौहर, खंडार व डागर।<br>• <b>ख्याल</b> तुलनात्मक रूप से मुक्त व अलंकृत रूप है, <b>ठुमरी</b> उपशास्त्रीय शैली की है, तथा <b>टप्पा</b> अपने तेज लड़खड़ाते स्वर-समूहों के लिए जाना जाता है।<br>• ध्रुपद <b>मुगल दरबार</b> से घनिष्ठ रूप से जुड़ा है, जहाँ मानसिंह तोमर तथा बाद में तानसेन ने इसी रूप में रचनाएँ कीं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000074215","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Himalayan River System","question":{"en":"Which of the following places does the Chenab river originate? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"चिनाब नदी निम्नलिखित में से किस स्थान से निकलती है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Lahual valley","hi":"लाहौल घाटी"},"2":{"en":"Near Rohtang Pass","hi":"रोहतांग दर्रे के निकट"},"3":{"en":"Near Manasarovar Lake","hi":"मानसरोवर झील के निकट"},"4":{"en":"Verinag","hi":"वेरीनाग"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Lahual valley</b><br>The <b>Chenab</b> rises in the <b>Lahaul valley</b> of Himachal Pradesh, where its two source streams, the <b>Chandra</b> and the <b>Bhaga</b>, meet near <b>Tandi</b>. It is the largest tributary of the Indus and is known as the <b>Chandrabhaga</b> in its upper course.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>Beas</b> originates near <b>Rohtang Pass</b>, not the Chenab, while the <b>Satluj</b> comes from Rakas Tal near Manasarovar and the <b>Jhelum</b> from Verinag in the Kashmir valley.<br>• The Chenab is about <b>960 km</b> long and is the <b>largest tributary of the Indus</b> in terms of discharge within India.<br>• Major projects on it are <b>Salal, Baglihar, Dulhasti and Ratle</b>, and it is famous for the world's highest railway bridge at <b>Kauri</b> in Reasi district.<br>• It flows through Jammu and Kashmir and Punjab before entering Pakistan, where it joins the Satluj at <b>Panjnad</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – लाहौल घाटी</b><br><b>चिनाब</b> नदी हिमाचल प्रदेश की <b>लाहौल घाटी</b> से निकलती है, जहाँ इसकी दो उद्गम धाराएँ <b>चंद्रा</b> व <b>भागा</b> <b>तांडी</b> के निकट मिलती हैं। यह सिंधु की सबसे बड़ी सहायक नदी है तथा ऊपरी भाग में <b>चंद्रभागा</b> कहलाती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>ब्यास</b> <b>रोहतांग दर्रे</b> के निकट से निकलती है, चिनाब से नहीं, जबकि <b>सतलुज</b> मानसरोवर के निकट राकस ताल से तथा <b>झेलम</b> कश्मीर घाटी के वेरीनाग से निकलती है।<br>• चिनाब लगभग <b>960 किमी</b> लंबी है और भारत में विसर्जन के आधार पर सिंधु की <b>सबसे बड़ी सहायक नदी</b> है।<br>• इस पर <b>सलाल, बगलिहार, दुलहस्ती व रातले</b> प्रमुख परियोजनाएँ हैं, तथा रियासी जिले में <b>कौड़ी</b> पर विश्व का सबसे ऊँचा रेल पुल बना है।<br>• यह जम्मू-कश्मीर व पंजाब से बहकर पाकिस्तान में प्रवेश करती है और वहाँ <b>पंजनद</b> पर सतलुज में मिलती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000074216","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Mahajanapadas","question":{"en":"Which Mahajanapada was located at the modern location of Munger and Bhagalpur with its capital at Champa? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कौन-सा महाजनपद वर्तमान मुंगेर व भागलपुर के स्थान पर स्थित था और जिसकी राजधानी चंपा थी? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The Vatsa Mahajanapada","hi":"वत्स महाजनपद"},"2":{"en":"The Anga Mahajanapada","hi":"अंग महाजनपद"},"3":{"en":"The Magadh Mahajanapada","hi":"मगध महाजनपद"},"4":{"en":"The Kasi Mahajanapada","hi":"काशी महाजनपद"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – The Anga Mahajanapada</b><br>The <b>Anga Mahajanapada</b> covered the present-day districts of <b>Munger and Bhagalpur</b> in Bihar, and its capital was <b>Champa</b>, situated on the bank of the Champa river.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• In the 6th century BCE there were <b>16 Mahajanapadas</b>, mentioned in the <b>Anguttara Nikaya</b> of the Buddhist canon.<br>• <b>Magadha</b> had its capital at <b>Rajgir</b> and later <b>Pataliputra</b>, <b>Vatsa</b> at <b>Kaushambi</b> and <b>Kasi</b> at <b>Varanasi</b>.<br>• Anga was a rival of Magadha and was eventually annexed by <b>Bimbisara</b> of Magadha.<br>• The other important Mahajanapadas were Avanti (Ujjain), Kosala (Sravasti), Vajji (Vaishali) and Gandhara (Taxila).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – अंग महाजनपद</b><br><b>अंग महाजनपद</b> बिहार के वर्तमान <b>मुंगेर व भागलपुर</b> जिलों में फैला था और इसकी राजधानी <b>चंपा</b> थी, जो चंपा नदी के तट पर स्थित थी।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• छठी शताब्दी ईसा पूर्व में <b>16 महाजनपद</b> थे, जिनका उल्लेख बौद्ध ग्रंथ <b>अंगुत्तर निकाय</b> में मिलता है।<br>• <b>मगध</b> की राजधानी <b>राजगीर</b> तथा बाद में <b>पाटलिपुत्र</b>, <b>वत्स</b> की <b>कौशांबी</b> और <b>काशी</b> की <b>वाराणसी</b> थी।<br>• अंग मगध का प्रतिद्वंद्वी था और अंततः मगध के <b>बिंबिसार</b> ने इसे अपने राज्य में मिला लिया।<br>• अन्य प्रमुख महाजनपद अवंति (उज्जैन), कोसल (श्रावस्ती), वज्जि (वैशाली) तथा गांधार (तक्षशिला) थे।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000074217","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: President and Vice President of India","question":{"en":"Under Article 65 of the Constitution of India, who acts as President when a vacancy occurs due to death, resignation, or removal of the President? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारत के संविधान के अनुच्छेद 65 के अंतर्गत, राष्ट्रपति की मृत्यु, त्यागपत्र या पदच्युति के कारण रिक्ति होने पर राष्ट्रपति के रूप में कौन कार्य करता है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Prime Minister","hi":"प्रधानमंत्री"},"2":{"en":"Chief Justice of India","hi":"भारत के मुख्य न्यायाधीश"},"3":{"en":"Vice-President","hi":"उपराष्ट्रपति"},"4":{"en":"Speaker of Lok Sabha","hi":"लोकसभा अध्यक्ष"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Vice-President</b><br>Under <b>Article 65</b>, when a vacancy arises in the office of the President by <b>death, resignation, removal or otherwise</b>, the <b>Vice-President</b> discharges the functions of the President until a new President is elected.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The election to fill such a vacancy must be held within <b>six months</b> as required by <b>Article 62</b>, and the Vice-President can act for that maximum period.<br>• Under <b>Article 64</b> the Vice-President is the <b>ex officio Chairman of the Rajya Sabha</b>, and under Article 63 he is the second-highest constitutional office holder.<br>• When the President is temporarily unable to discharge his functions, the Vice-President acts under <b>Article 65(2)</b>.<br>• The <b>Chief Justice of India</b> administers the oath to the President under Article 60, and the <b>Speaker of the Lok Sabha</b> has no role in the presidential succession.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – उपराष्ट्रपति</b><br><b>अनुच्छेद 65</b> के अंतर्गत जब <b>मृत्यु, त्यागपत्र, पदच्युति अथवा अन्य कारण</b> से राष्ट्रपति के पद में रिक्ति होती है, तो <b>उपराष्ट्रपति</b> नए राष्ट्रपति के निर्वाचन तक राष्ट्रपति के कार्य करता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• ऐसी रिक्ति को भरने हेतु <b>अनुच्छेद 62</b> के अनुसार <b>छह माह</b> के भीतर निर्वाचन होना आवश्यक है और उपराष्ट्रपति अधिकतम उतनी ही अवधि तक कार्य कर सकते हैं।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 64</b> के अंतर्गत उपराष्ट्रपति <b>राज्यसभा के पदेन सभापति</b> होते हैं, तथा अनुच्छेद 63 के अनुसार यह दूसरा सर्वोच्च संवैधानिक पद है।<br>• जब राष्ट्रपति अस्थायी रूप से अपने कार्य करने में असमर्थ हों, तब <b>अनुच्छेद 65(2)</b> के अंतर्गत उपराष्ट्रपति कार्य करते हैं।<br>• राष्ट्रपति को शपथ <b>भारत के मुख्य न्यायाधीश</b> अनुच्छेद 60 के अंतर्गत दिलाते हैं, तथा <b>लोकसभा अध्यक्ष</b> की राष्ट्रपति के उत्तराधिकार में कोई भूमिका नहीं है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000074218","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Agriculture","question":{"en":"Which crop is included in the Rabi season in Northern India? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"उत्तरी भारत में रबी मौसम में कौन-सी फसल सम्मिलित है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Cotton","hi":"कपास"},"2":{"en":"Bajra","hi":"बाजरा"},"3":{"en":"Gram","hi":"चना"},"4":{"en":"Maize","hi":"मक्का"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Gram</b><br><b>Gram (chana)</b> is a <b>Rabi</b> crop. Rabi crops are sown in <b>October to December</b> and harvested in <b>April to June</b>, and they need a cool growing season with a warm, dry ripening period.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The main Rabi crops are <b>wheat, barley, gram, mustard, peas and lentil (masur)</b>; Punjab, Haryana and western Uttar Pradesh are the leading wheat-growing areas.<br>• <b>Cotton, bajra and maize</b> are <b>Kharif</b> crops, sown with the onset of the monsoon in June and harvested in October.<br>• <b>Zaid</b> is a short third season for crops such as watermelon, muskmelon, cucumber and fodder.<br>• India is the largest producer of <b>gram (chickpea)</b> in the world, with Madhya Pradesh the leading state.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – चना</b><br><b>चना</b> एक <b>रबी</b> फसल है। रबी फसलें <b>अक्टूबर से दिसंबर</b> में बोई जाती हैं और <b>अप्रैल से जून</b> में काटी जाती हैं; इन्हें बढ़वार के समय ठंडा तथा पकने के समय गर्म व शुष्क मौसम चाहिए।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• प्रमुख रबी फसलें <b>गेहूँ, जौ, चना, सरसों, मटर व मसूर</b> हैं; पंजाब, हरियाणा तथा पश्चिमी उत्तर प्रदेश गेहूँ के प्रमुख क्षेत्र हैं।<br>• <b>कपास, बाजरा व मक्का</b> <b>खरीफ</b> फसलें हैं, जो जून में मानसून के आगमन के साथ बोई और अक्टूबर में काटी जाती हैं।<br>• <b>जायद</b> तीसरा संक्षिप्त मौसम है, जिसमें तरबूज, खरबूजा, ककड़ी तथा चारा उगाया जाता है।<br>• भारत विश्व में <b>चने</b> का सबसे बड़ा उत्पादक है, जिसमें मध्य प्रदेश अग्रणी राज्य है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000074219","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Basics of Economy","question":{"en":"Which of the following industries is an example of a Basic Industry? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा उद्योग आधारभूत (बेसिक) उद्योग का उदाहरण है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Toothpaste industry","hi":"टूथपेस्ट उद्योग"},"2":{"en":"Soap industry","hi":"साबुन उद्योग"},"3":{"en":"Iron and steel industry","hi":"लोहा एवं इस्पात उद्योग"},"4":{"en":"Textiles and Apparel industry","hi":"वस्त्र एवं परिधान उद्योग"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Iron and steel industry</b><br>A <b>basic industry</b> produces the inputs, machinery or raw material that other industries need, and the <b>iron and steel industry</b> is its classic example because steel feeds construction, engineering, automobile and defence production.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Basic or <b>key industries</b> include iron and steel, cement, aluminium, heavy chemicals, fertiliser and machine tools.<br>• Toothpaste, soap and textiles are <b>consumer goods industries</b>, as they make goods for direct use by households.<br>• Industries are also classed by ownership (public, private, joint, cooperative) and by the weight of raw material used (<b>agro-based and mineral-based</b>).<br>• India's first iron and steel plant of the modern era was set up at <b>Jamshedpur (TISCO) in 1907</b>, followed by Bhilai, Rourkela and Durgapur in the Second Plan.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – लोहा एवं इस्पात उद्योग</b><br><b>आधारभूत (बेसिक) उद्योग</b> वह होता है जो अन्य उद्योगों हेतु आवश्यक कच्चा माल, मशीनरी या इनपुट तैयार करता है; <b>लोहा एवं इस्पात उद्योग</b> इसका प्रमुख उदाहरण है, क्योंकि इस्पात निर्माण, अभियांत्रिकी, वाहन व रक्षा उत्पादन का आधार है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• आधारभूत अथवा <b>मूल उद्योगों</b> में लोहा-इस्पात, सीमेंट, एल्युमिनियम, भारी रसायन, उर्वरक तथा मशीन उपकरण सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• टूथपेस्ट, साबुन व वस्त्र <b>उपभोक्ता वस्तु उद्योग</b> हैं, क्योंकि ये घरों के प्रत्यक्ष उपयोग की वस्तुएँ बनाते हैं।<br>• उद्योगों को स्वामित्व (सार्वजनिक, निजी, संयुक्त, सहकारी) तथा कच्चे माल के भार (<b>कृषि आधारित व खनिज आधारित</b>) के आधार पर भी वर्गीकृत किया जाता है।<br>• आधुनिक युग का भारत का पहला लोहा-इस्पात संयंत्र <b>1907 में जमशेदपुर (टिस्को)</b> में लगा, इसके बाद दूसरी योजना में भिलाई, राउरकेला व दुर्गापुर बने।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000074220","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"In which year did the National Games of India officially adopt its current name (shifting from \"Indian Olympic Games\")? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारत के राष्ट्रीय खेलों ने किस वर्ष आधिकारिक रूप से अपना वर्तमान नाम अपनाया (\"इंडियन ओलंपिक खेलों\" से परिवर्तित)? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1924"},"2":{"en":"1940"},"3":{"en":"1947"},"4":{"en":"1952"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – 1940</b><br>The Indian Olympic Games, first held at <b>Lahore in 1924</b>, were officially renamed the <b>National Games</b> in <b>1940</b>, from the ninth edition of the Games.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>Indian Olympic Association</b> was formed in <b>1927</b> and is the body that organises the National Games.<br>• The National Games are held every two years and are hosted by a different state each time.<br>• The modern Olympic-style National Games began at <b>New Delhi in 1985</b>, and the 2025 edition was hosted by <b>Uttarakhand</b>.<br>• <b>1924</b> is the year of the first Indian Olympic Games, which makes it the closest wrong option.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – 1940</b><br><b>1924 में लाहौर</b> में पहली बार आयोजित इंडियन ओलंपिक खेलों का नाम <b>1940</b> में आधिकारिक रूप से <b>राष्ट्रीय खेल</b> कर दिया गया। यह नाम <b>1940</b> में खेलों के नवें संस्करण से आधिकारिक रूप से अपनाया गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>भारतीय ओलंपिक संघ</b> की स्थापना <b>1927</b> में हुई और राष्ट्रीय खेलों का आयोजन यही संस्था करती है।<br>• राष्ट्रीय खेल प्रत्येक दो वर्ष में होते हैं और प्रत्येक बार भिन्न राज्य इनकी मेज़बानी करता है।<br>• ओलंपिक शैली के आधुनिक राष्ट्रीय खेल <b>1985 में नई दिल्ली</b> से आरंभ हुए, तथा 2025 का संस्करण <b>उत्तराखंड</b> में आयोजित हुआ।<br>• <b>1924</b> प्रथम इंडियन ओलंपिक खेलों का वर्ष है, इसीलिए यह यहाँ निकटतम गलत विकल्प है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000074221","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Himalayas","question":{"en":"Which two geological zones are separated by the Main Central Thrust? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"मुख्य केंद्रीय क्षेप (Main Central Thrust) किन दो भूवैज्ञानिक क्षेत्रों को अलग करता है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Plains and Shiwaliks","hi":"मैदान एवं शिवालिक"},"2":{"en":"Greater Himalayas and Trans-Himalayas","hi":"वृहद् हिमालय एवं ट्रांस-हिमालय"},"3":{"en":"Greater and Lesser Himalayas","hi":"वृहद् एवं लघु हिमालय"},"4":{"en":"Shiwaliks and Lesser Himalayas","hi":"शिवालिक एवं लघु हिमालय"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Greater and Lesser Himalayas</b><br>The <b>Main Central Thrust (MCT)</b> is the great boundary fault that separates the <b>Greater Himalayas (Himadri)</b> in the north from the <b>Lesser Himalayas (Himachal)</b> in the south.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>Main Boundary Thrust (MBT)</b> separates the Lesser Himalayas from the <b>Shiwaliks</b>, and the <b>Himalayan Front Fault</b> separates the Shiwaliks from the northern plains.<br>• The <b>Indus-Tsangpo Suture Zone</b> marks the boundary between the Trans-Himalayas and the Greater Himalayas.<br>• The Himalayas are divided from south to north into the <b>Shiwaliks, Lesser Himalayas, Greater Himalayas and Trans-Himalayas</b>.<br>• These thrusts are active and are the reason for the frequent <b>earthquakes</b> along the Himalayan belt.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – वृहद् एवं लघु हिमालय</b><br><b>मुख्य केंद्रीय क्षेप (Main Central Thrust)</b> वह बड़ा सीमांत भ्रंश है जो उत्तर में <b>वृहद् हिमालय (हिमाद्रि)</b> को दक्षिण के <b>लघु हिमालय (हिमाचल)</b> से अलग करता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>मुख्य सीमांत क्षेप (MBT)</b> लघु हिमालय को <b>शिवालिक</b> से अलग करता है, तथा हिमालयी फ्रंट भ्रंश शिवालिक को उत्तरी मैदानों से।<br>• <b>सिंधु-त्सांगपो सीवन क्षेत्र</b> ट्रांस-हिमालय व वृहद् हिमालय के बीच की सीमा बनाता है।<br>• हिमालय दक्षिण से उत्तर की ओर <b>शिवालिक, लघु हिमालय, वृहद् हिमालय तथा ट्रांस-हिमालय</b> में विभाजित है।<br>• ये क्षेप सक्रिय हैं और हिमालयी पट्टी में आने वाले बार-बार के <b>भूकंपों</b> का कारण हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000074222","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: State Legislature","question":{"en":"A State Legislature in India is said to be bicameral when it consists of: [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारत में किसी राज्य के विधानमंडल को द्विसदनीय कहा जाता है जब उसमें सम्मिलित होते हैं: [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Legislative Assembly and Legislative Council","hi":"विधान सभा एवं विधान परिषद"},"2":{"en":"Governor and Council of Ministers","hi":"राज्यपाल एवं मंत्रिपरिषद"},"3":{"en":"High Court and Assembly","hi":"उच्च न्यायालय एवं विधान सभा"},"4":{"en":"Governor and Assembly","hi":"राज्यपाल एवं विधान सभा"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Legislative Assembly and Legislative Council</b><br>A State Legislature is <b>bicameral</b> when it has two Houses - the <b>Legislative Assembly (Vidhan Sabha)</b>, the directly elected lower House, and the <b>Legislative Council (Vidhan Parishad)</b>, the permanent upper House.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Only <b>six states</b> have Legislative Councils - Uttar Pradesh, Bihar, Maharashtra, Karnataka, Andhra Pradesh and Telangana.<br>• A Legislative Council is created or abolished by Parliament under <b>Article 169</b> on a resolution passed by the Assembly by a special majority.<br>• The strength of a Council cannot exceed <b>one-third of the strength of the Assembly</b>, and it is a permanent House with one-third of members retiring every two years.<br>• The <b>Governor</b> is part of the Legislature but is not a House, and the <b>Council of Ministers</b> runs the executive, not the legislature.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – विधान सभा एवं विधान परिषद</b><br>किसी राज्य का विधानमंडल तब <b>द्विसदनीय</b> कहलाता है जब उसमें दो सदन हों - प्रत्यक्ष निर्वाचित निम्न सदन <b>विधान सभा</b> तथा स्थायी उच्च सदन <b>विधान परिषद</b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• केवल <b>छह राज्यों</b> में विधान परिषद है - उत्तर प्रदेश, बिहार, महाराष्ट्र, कर्नाटक, आंध्र प्रदेश तथा तेलंगाना।<br>• विधान परिषद का गठन या उत्सादन संसद <b>अनुच्छेद 169</b> के अंतर्गत विधान सभा के विशेष बहुमत प्रस्ताव पर करती है।<br>• परिषद की सदस्य संख्या विधान सभा की संख्या के <b>एक-तिहाई</b> से अधिक नहीं हो सकती, तथा यह स्थायी सदन है जिसके एक-तिहाई सदस्य प्रत्येक दो वर्ष में सेवानिवृत्त होते हैं।<br>• <b>राज्यपाल</b> विधानमंडल का अंग है, परंतु सदन नहीं, तथा <b>मंत्रिपरिषद</b> कार्यपालिका चलाती है, विधानमंडल नहीं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000074223","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: National Parks","question":{"en":"Consider the following statements about Chhari-Dhand wetland:<br>1. It is located in the Kutch district of Gujarat and was designated as a Ramsar site in January 2026.<br>2. The wetland is home to endangered species such as the Dalmatian Pelican, Oriental Darter, and Indian Skimmer<br>Which of the statements given above is/are <b>correct</b>? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"छड़ी-ढांड आर्द्रभूमि के संबंध में निम्नलिखित कथनों पर विचार कीजिए:<br>1. यह गुजरात के कच्छ जिले में स्थित है तथा जनवरी 2026 में इसे रामसर स्थल घोषित किया गया।<br>2. यह आर्द्रभूमि डालमेशियन पेलिकन, ओरिएंटल डार्टर तथा भारतीय स्किमर जैसी संकटग्रस्त प्रजातियों का आवास है।<br>उपर्युक्त कथनों में से कौन-सा/से <b>सही</b> है/हैं? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only 1","hi":"केवल 1"},"2":{"en":"Only 2","hi":"केवल 2"},"3":{"en":"Both 1 and 2","hi":"1 और 2 दोनों"},"4":{"en":"Neither 1 nor 2","hi":"न तो 1, न ही 2"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Both 1 and 2</b><br><b>Chhari-Dhand</b> is a seasonal wetland conservation reserve in the <b>Banni grasslands of Kutch district, Gujarat</b>, and it was designated a <b>Ramsar site on 31 January 2026</b>, becoming India's 98th Ramsar site and Gujarat's fifth. The wetland hosts <b>Dalmatian pelican, Oriental darter, Indian skimmer</b> and other threatened birds, so both statements are correct.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Chhari-Dhand was declared Gujarat's first <b>Conservation Reserve in 2008</b> under the Wild Life (Protection) Act, 1972, and covers about <b>22,700 hectares</b>.<br>• It supports more than <b>250 bird species</b> and is an important stopover on the <b>Central Asian Flyway</b>; over 40,000 common cranes have been recorded here at one time.<br>• The Ramsar Convention, signed in <b>1971 at Ramsar in Iran</b>, is an intergovernmental treaty for the conservation and wise use of wetlands.<br>• With this addition, India's tally of Ramsar sites rose to <b>98</b>, the highest in Asia.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 1 और 2 दोनों</b><br><b>छड़ी-ढांड</b> गुजरात के <b>कच्छ जिले की बन्नी घासभूमि</b> में स्थित मौसमी आर्द्रभूमि संरक्षण रिज़र्व है और <b>31 जनवरी 2026</b> को इसे रामसर स्थल घोषित किया गया; यह भारत का 98वाँ तथा गुजरात का पाँचवाँ रामसर स्थल बना। यहाँ <b>डालमेशियन पेलिकन, ओरिएंटल डार्टर, भारतीय स्किमर</b> जैसे संकटग्रस्त पक्षी पाए जाते हैं, अतः दोनों कथन सही हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• छड़ी-ढांड को वन्य जीव (संरक्षण) अधिनियम, 1972 के अंतर्गत <b>2008</b> में गुजरात का प्रथम <b>संरक्षण रिज़र्व</b> घोषित किया गया था और यह लगभग <b>22,700 हेक्टेयर</b> में फैला है।<br>• यहाँ <b>250 से अधिक पक्षी प्रजातियाँ</b> हैं और यह <b>मध्य एशियाई उड़ान मार्ग</b> का महत्वपूर्ण पड़ाव है; एक समय यहाँ 40,000 से अधिक सारस देखे गए हैं।<br>• रामसर अभिसमय <b>1971 में ईरान के रामसर</b> में हस्ताक्षरित एक अंतरसरकारी संधि है, जो आर्द्रभूमियों के संरक्षण व विवेकपूर्ण उपयोग से संबंधित है।<br>• इसके जुड़ने से भारत के रामसर स्थलों की संख्या <b>98</b> हो गई, जो एशिया में सर्वाधिक है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000074224","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Making of Constitution","question":{"en":"The term \"constitution\" originates from the Latin word constituere. What does constituere mean? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"\"संविधान (constitution)\" शब्द लैटिन के constituere से उत्पन्न हुआ है। constituere का अर्थ क्या है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To rule or govern","hi":"शासन करना"},"2":{"en":"To divide or separate","hi":"विभाजित करना"},"3":{"en":"To establish or set up","hi":"स्थापित करना"},"4":{"en":"To protect or defend","hi":"संरक्षण देना"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – To establish or set up</b><br>The word <b>constitution</b> comes from the Latin <b>constituere</b>, which means <b>to establish, to set up or to frame</b>. It therefore denotes the fundamental law by which a state is set up and organised.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Constitution of India was adopted by the <b>Constituent Assembly on 26 November 1949</b> and came into force on <b>26 January 1950</b>.<br>• It was framed by a Constituent Assembly set up under the <b>Cabinet Mission Plan, 1946</b>, with <b>Dr B. R. Ambedkar</b> as Chairman of the Drafting Committee.<br>• The <b>Preamble</b> declares India a Sovereign, Socialist, Secular, Democratic Republic and was amended by the <b>42nd Amendment Act, 1976</b>.<br>• The original Constitution had <b>395 Articles, 22 Parts and 8 Schedules</b>, and it is the longest written constitution in the world.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – स्थापित करना</b><br><b>संविधान (constitution)</b> शब्द लैटिन <b>constituere</b> से बना है, जिसका अर्थ <b>स्थापित करना, गठित करना अथवा निर्माण करना</b> है। इसलिए यह उस मूल विधि को दर्शाता है जिससे राज्य की स्थापना व संगठन होता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारत का संविधान <b>26 नवंबर 1949</b> को संविधान सभा द्वारा अंगीकृत हुआ और <b>26 जनवरी 1950</b> को लागू हुआ।<br>• इसे <b>कैबिनेट मिशन योजना, 1946</b> के अंतर्गत गठित संविधान सभा ने बनाया, जिसकी प्रारूप समिति के अध्यक्ष <b>डॉ. बी. आर. आंबेडकर</b> थे।<br>• <b>प्रस्तावना</b> भारत को संपूर्ण प्रभुत्व-संपन्न, समाजवादी, पंथनिरपेक्ष, लोकतंत्रात्मक गणराज्य घोषित करती है तथा इसे <b>42वें संशोधन अधिनियम, 1976</b> से संशोधित किया गया।<br>• मूल संविधान में <b>395 अनुच्छेद, 22 भाग व 8 अनुसूचियाँ</b> थीं और यह विश्व का सबसे लंबा लिखित संविधान है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000074225","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"What was the primary objective of token privatisation or disinvestment under the economic reforms of 1991? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"1991 के आर्थिक सुधारों के अंतर्गत टोकन निजीकरण अथवा विनिवेश का प्राथमिक उद्देश्य क्या था? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Expanding public ownership across industries","hi":"उद्योगों में सार्वजनिक स्वामित्व का विस्तार"},"2":{"en":"Obtaining revenue to reduce budget deficits","hi":"बजट घाटे को घटाने हेतु राजस्व प्राप्ति"},"3":{"en":"Increasing industrial licensing requirements nationally","hi":"देशव्यापी औद्योगिक लाइसेंस आवश्यकताओं में वृद्धि"},"4":{"en":"Promoting administrative control over prices","hi":"कीमतों पर प्रशासनिक नियंत्रण को बढ़ावा"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Obtaining revenue to reduce budget deficits</b><br>In <b>token disinvestment</b> the government sold only a small part of its stake in public sector units. The main purpose was to <b>raise resources and reduce the fiscal deficit</b>, not to transfer management control.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Disinvestment began in <b>1991-92</b>, and a separate <b>Department of Disinvestment</b> was created in 1999, later renamed <b>DIPAM</b> in 2017.<br>• <b>Strategic disinvestment</b> means sale of a majority stake along with transfer of management control, as in the case of <b>Air India</b> in 2022.<br>• The <b>New Industrial Policy of July 1991</b> cut the number of industries reserved for the public sector and abolished licensing for most industries.<br>• Major disinvestments include the <b>LIC IPO (2022)</b> and offers for sale in CPSEs through the stock exchange mechanism.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – बजट घाटे को घटाने हेतु राजस्व प्राप्ति</b><br><b>टोकन विनिवेश</b> में सरकार सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र की इकाइयों में अपनी केवल छोटी हिस्सेदारी बेचती थी। इसका मुख्य उद्देश्य <b>संसाधन जुटाना तथा राजकोषीय घाटा घटाना</b> था, प्रबंधन नियंत्रण का हस्तांतरण नहीं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• विनिवेश <b>1991-92</b> में आरंभ हुआ और 1999 में पृथक <b>विनिवेश विभाग</b> बना, जिसे 2017 में <b>DIPAM</b> नाम दिया गया।<br>• <b>रणनीतिक विनिवेश</b> का अर्थ बहुमत हिस्सेदारी के साथ प्रबंधन नियंत्रण का हस्तांतरण है, जैसे 2022 में <b>एयर इंडिया</b> के मामले में।<br>• <b>जुलाई 1991 की नई औद्योगिक नीति</b> ने सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र हेतु आरक्षित उद्योगों की संख्या घटाई तथा अधिकांश उद्योगों हेतु लाइसेंसिंग समाप्त की।<br>• प्रमुख विनिवेशों में <b>LIC का आईपीओ (2022)</b> तथा स्टॉक एक्सचेंज तंत्र से CPSEs के ऑफर फॉर सेल सम्मिलित हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000074226","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"In 1991, what was the primary aim of introducing liberalisation? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"1991 में उदारीकरण लागू करने का प्राथमिक उद्देश्य क्या था? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Restricting more sectors of economy","hi":"अर्थव्यवस्था के अधिक क्षेत्रों को प्रतिबंधित करना"},"2":{"en":"Opening up various sectors of economy","hi":"अर्थव्यवस्था के विभिन्न क्षेत्रों को खोलना"},"3":{"en":"Nationalising more industries","hi":"अधिक उद्योगों का राष्ट्रीयकरण"},"4":{"en":"Reducing foreign investment","hi":"विदेशी निवेश कम करना"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Opening up various sectors of economy</b><br><b>Liberalisation</b> in 1991 aimed at freeing the economy from excessive state control by <b>opening up various sectors</b> to private and foreign investment, removing licences and reducing bureaucratic restrictions.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The reforms followed the <b>balance-of-payments crisis of 1991</b>, when foreign exchange reserves fell to about two weeks of imports and India pledged gold to raise funds.<br>• The <b>New Industrial Policy of 24 July 1991</b> abolished industrial licensing for all but a handful of industries and raised the foreign equity limit to <b>51 per cent</b> in many sectors.<br>• Liberalisation was accompanied by <b>privatisation</b> (disinvestment) and <b>globalisation</b> (integration with the world economy), together called the LPG reforms.<br>• The rupee was devalued in <b>July 1991</b>, and trade policy was freed through the Export-Import Policy of 1992.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – अर्थव्यवस्था के विभिन्न क्षेत्रों को खोलना</b><br>1991 के <b>उदारीकरण</b> का उद्देश्य अर्थव्यवस्था को अत्यधिक राज्य नियंत्रण से मुक्त करते हुए <b>विभिन्न क्षेत्रों को</b> निजी व विदेशी निवेश हेतु <b>खोलना</b>, लाइसेंस हटाना तथा नौकरशाही बाधाएँ घटाना था।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सुधार <b>1991 के भुगतान संतुलन संकट</b> के बाद हुए, जब विदेशी मुद्रा भंडार लगभग दो सप्ताह के आयात तक रह गया था और भारत ने धन जुटाने हेतु स्वर्ण गिरवी रखा।<br>• <b>24 जुलाई 1991 की नई औद्योगिक नीति</b> ने कुछ ही उद्योगों को छोड़कर औद्योगिक लाइसेंसिंग समाप्त की तथा कई क्षेत्रों में विदेशी पूँजी की सीमा <b>51 प्रतिशत</b> की।<br>• उदारीकरण के साथ <b>निजीकरण</b> (विनिवेश) तथा <b>वैश्वीकरण</b> (विश्व अर्थव्यवस्था से एकीकरण) चले, जिन्हें सम्मिलित रूप से LPG सुधार कहा जाता है।<br>• <b>जुलाई 1991</b> में रुपये का अवमूल्यन हुआ तथा 1992 की निर्यात-आयात नीति से व्यापार नीति को मुक्त किया गया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000074227","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Human Geography","question":{"en":"The shift of a society from high mortality and high fertility rates to low mortality and low fertility rates is known as: [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"किसी समाज का उच्च मृत्यु-दर व उच्च प्रजनन-दर से निम्न मृत्यु-दर व निम्न प्रजनन-दर की ओर परिवर्तन कहलाता है: [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Occupational mobility","hi":"व्यावसायिक गतिशीलता"},"2":{"en":"Rural urbanisation","hi":"ग्रामीण नगरीकरण"},"3":{"en":"Demographic transition","hi":"जनसांख्यिकीय संक्रमण"},"4":{"en":"Population stagnation","hi":"जनसंख्या ठहराव"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Demographic transition</b><br>The <b>demographic transition</b> is the historical shift of a population from the <b>high birth rate and high death rate</b> stage to the <b>low birth rate and low death rate</b> stage as a society develops.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The theory has <b>four to five stages</b>; in stage 2 mortality falls first and population grows rapidly, while in stage 3 fertility begins to fall.<br>• India is usually placed in <b>stage 3</b> of the transition, with a falling birth rate and a large working-age population, giving it a <b>demographic dividend</b>.<br>• The <b>sex ratio</b> of India was 943 females per 1,000 males and the literacy rate 74.04 per cent in the <b>2011 Census</b>.<br>• <b>Occupational mobility</b> refers to change of occupation, and <b>population stagnation</b> is a stationary stage where births and deaths are nearly equal.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – जनसांख्यिकीय संक्रमण</b><br><b>जनसांख्यिकीय संक्रमण</b> विकास के साथ किसी जनसंख्या के <b>उच्च जन्म-दर व उच्च मृत्यु-दर</b> वाले चरण से <b>निम्न जन्म-दर व निम्न मृत्यु-दर</b> वाले चरण की ओर ऐतिहासिक परिवर्तन को कहते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इस सिद्धांत में <b>चार से पाँच चरण</b> हैं; दूसरे चरण में मृत्यु-दर पहले घटती है और जनसंख्या तेजी से बढ़ती है, तथा तीसरे चरण में प्रजनन-दर घटने लगती है।<br>• भारत सामान्यतः संक्रमण के <b>तीसरे चरण</b> में माना जाता है, जहाँ जन्म-दर घट रही है और कार्यशील आयु की बड़ी जनसंख्या के कारण <b>जनसांख्यिकीय लाभांश</b> मिल रहा है।<br>• <b>2011 की जनगणना</b> में भारत का <b>लिंगानुपात</b> प्रति 1,000 पुरुषों पर 943 महिलाएँ तथा साक्षरता दर 74.04 प्रतिशत थी।<br>• <b>व्यावसायिक गतिशीलता</b> व्यवसाय परिवर्तन को दर्शाती है, तथा <b>जनसंख्या ठहराव</b> वह स्थिर अवस्था है जिसमें जन्म व मृत्यु लगभग बराबर होते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000074228","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Which of the following best describes the principal subject matter of the Charaka Samhita? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा चरक संहिता के प्रमुख विषय का सर्वोत्तम वर्णन करता है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Surgery, anatomy, and surgical procedures","hi":"शल्य चिकित्सा, शरीर रचना तथा शल्य प्रक्रियाएँ"},"2":{"en":"Medicine, diagnosis, and internal medicine","hi":"चिकित्सा, निदान तथा आंतरिक चिकित्सा"},"3":{"en":"Astronomy, planetary studies, and celestial observations","hi":"खगोल विज्ञान, ग्रह अध्ययन तथा आकाशीय प्रेक्षण"},"4":{"en":"Warfare, military tactics, and strategic planning","hi":"युद्ध, सैन्य रणनीति तथा सामरिक योजना"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Medicine, diagnosis, and internal medicine</b><br>The <b>Charaka Samhita</b> is the foundational text of <b>Ayurveda</b> and deals with <b>medicine, diagnosis, pathology and internal medicine</b> (kayachikitsa). It is attributed to <b>Charaka</b> and later revised by Dridhabala.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Charaka Samhita has <b>eight sections (sthanas)</b>, including Sutra, Nidana, Vimana, Sharira, Indriya, Chikitsa, Kalpa and Siddhi.<br>• <b>Surgery, anatomy and surgical procedures</b> are the subject of the <b>Sushruta Samhita</b>, whose author Sushruta is called the father of surgery.<br>• Charaka is traditionally regarded as the court physician of the <b>Kushana ruler Kanishka</b>.<br>• Ancient Indian medicine also appears in the <b>Atharvaveda</b>, and the Charaka and Sushruta Samhitas were translated into Arabic and Persian in medieval times.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – चिकित्सा, निदान तथा आंतरिक चिकित्सा</b><br><b>चरक संहिता</b> <b>आयुर्वेद</b> का आधारभूत ग्रंथ है और इसमें <b>चिकित्सा, निदान, रोग-विज्ञान तथा आंतरिक चिकित्सा (कायचिकित्सा)</b> का वर्णन है। इसका श्रेय <b>चरक</b> को है और बाद में दृढ़बल ने इसका पुनःसंपादन किया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• चरक संहिता के <b>आठ स्थान</b> हैं - सूत्र, निदान, विमान, शरीर, इंद्रिय, चिकित्सा, कल्प तथा सिद्धि।<br>• <b>शल्य चिकित्सा, शरीर रचना व शल्य प्रक्रियाएँ</b> <b>सुश्रुत संहिता</b> का विषय हैं, जिसके रचयिता सुश्रुत को शल्य चिकित्सा का जनक कहा जाता है।<br>• चरक को परंपरागत रूप से <b>कुषाण शासक कनिष्क</b> का राजवैद्य माना जाता है।<br>• प्राचीन भारतीय चिकित्सा का उल्लेख <b>अथर्ववेद</b> में भी है, तथा मध्यकाल में चरक व सुश्रुत संहिताओं का अरबी व फारसी में अनुवाद हुआ।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000074229","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Motion","question":{"en":"A particle performs simple harmonic motion with amplitude A. When its displacement from the mean position is \\(\\frac{A}{2}\\), what percentage of its total mechanical energy is kinetic energy? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कोई कण आयाम A के साथ सरल आवर्त गति करता है। जब माध्य स्थिति से इसका विस्थापन \\(\\frac{A}{2}\\) हो, तो इसकी कुल यांत्रिक ऊर्जा का कितना प्रतिशत गतिज ऊर्जा है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"25% of total","hi":"कुल का 25%"},"2":{"en":"50% of total","hi":"कुल का 50%"},"3":{"en":"75% of total","hi":"कुल का 75%"},"4":{"en":"100% of total","hi":"कुल का 100%"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 75% of total</b><br>For a particle in simple harmonic motion the total energy is \\(E = \\frac{1}{2}m\\omega^{2}A^{2}\\) and the potential energy at displacement \\(x\\) is \\(U = \\frac{1}{2}m\\omega^{2}x^{2}\\). At \\(x = \\frac{A}{2}\\), \\(U = \\frac{1}{4}E\\), so the kinetic energy is \\(E - U = \\frac{3}{4}E\\), that is <b>75 per cent</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• At the <b>mean position</b> the kinetic energy is maximum and the potential energy is zero; at the extreme position the reverse is true.<br>• Total mechanical energy in simple harmonic motion remains <b>constant</b> because the restoring force is conservative.<br>• The kinetic energy of a particle in simple harmonic motion is \\(K = \\frac{1}{2}m\\omega^{2}\\left(A^{2} - x^{2}\\right)\\), so it varies with the square of the displacement.<br>• Kinetic and potential energies each complete <b>two oscillations</b> in one period of the particle, so their average values are equal.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – कुल का 75%</b><br>सरल आवर्त गति में कुल ऊर्जा \\(E = \\frac{1}{2}m\\omega^{2}A^{2}\\) तथा विस्थापन \\(x\\) पर स्थितिज ऊर्जा \\(U = \\frac{1}{2}m\\omega^{2}x^{2}\\) होती है। \\(x = \\frac{A}{2}\\) पर \\(U = \\frac{1}{4}E\\), अतः गतिज ऊर्जा \\(E - U = \\frac{3}{4}E\\), अर्थात् <b>75 प्रतिशत</b> होगी।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>माध्य स्थिति</b> पर गतिज ऊर्जा अधिकतम तथा स्थितिज ऊर्जा शून्य होती है; चरम स्थिति पर विपरीत स्थिति होती है।<br>• सरल आवर्त गति में कुल यांत्रिक ऊर्जा <b>अचर</b> रहती है, क्योंकि प्रत्यानयन बल संरक्षी होता है।<br>• सरल आवर्त गति में कण की गतिज ऊर्जा \\(K = \\frac{1}{2}m\\omega^{2}\\left(A^{2} - x^{2}\\right)\\) होती है, अतः यह विस्थापन के वर्ग के अनुसार बदलती है।<br>• एक आवर्तकाल में गतिज व स्थितिज ऊर्जा प्रत्येक <b>दो दोलन</b> पूरे करती हैं, इसलिए इनके औसत मान समान होते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000074230","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Five Year Plan and Industrial Policy Resolution","question":{"en":"The Second Five-Year Plan was based on which economic model, and what was its primary objective? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दूसरी पंचवर्षीय योजना किस आर्थिक मॉडल पर आधारित थी और उसका प्राथमिक उद्देश्य क्या था? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Mahalanobis model; Rapid industrialization","hi":"महालनोबिस मॉडल; तीव्र औद्योगीकरण"},"2":{"en":"Harrod-Domar model; Agricultural development","hi":"हैरोड-डोमर मॉडल; कृषि विकास"},"3":{"en":"Keynesian model; Demand management","hi":"कीनेसियन मॉडल; माँग प्रबंधन"},"4":{"en":"Classical model; Trade expansion","hi":"चिरसम्मत मॉडल; व्यापार विस्तार"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Mahalanobis model; Rapid industrialization</b><br>The <b>Second Five-Year Plan (1956-61)</b> was framed on the <b>Mahalanobis model</b>, which gave priority to the <b>heavy and basic goods industries</b> for rapid industrialisation.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The plan targeted a growth rate of <b>4.5 per cent</b> and led to the setting up of the steel plants at <b>Bhilai, Rourkela and Durgapur</b>.<br>• The <b>First Five-Year Plan (1951-56)</b> was based on the <b>Harrod-Domar model</b> and concentrated on <b>agriculture</b>, especially irrigation and food production.<br>• The Second Plan followed the <b>Industrial Policy Resolution of 1956</b>, which divided industries into three schedules and gave the public sector a leading role.<br>• Its heavy-industry focus caused a shortage of consumer goods and a growing <b>food and foreign exchange crisis</b>, which shaped the Third Plan.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – महालनोबिस मॉडल; तीव्र औद्योगीकरण</b><br><b>दूसरी पंचवर्षीय योजना (1956-61)</b> <b>महालनोबिस मॉडल</b> पर आधारित थी, जिसने तीव्र औद्योगीकरण हेतु <b>भारी व आधारभूत वस्तु उद्योगों</b> को प्राथमिकता दी।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• योजना का लक्ष्य <b>4.5 प्रतिशत</b> वृद्धि दर था और इसी अवधि में <b>भिलाई, राउरकेला तथा दुर्गापुर</b> के इस्पात संयंत्र लगाए गए।<br>• <b>पहली पंचवर्षीय योजना (1951-56)</b> <b>हैरोड-डोमर मॉडल</b> पर आधारित थी और उसका ध्यान <b>कृषि</b>, विशेषकर सिंचाई व खाद्य उत्पादन पर था।<br>• दूसरी योजना <b>1956 के औद्योगिक नीति प्रस्ताव</b> के अनुसरण में थी, जिसने उद्योगों को तीन अनुसूचियों में बाँटकर सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र को अग्रणी भूमिका दी।<br>• भारी उद्योग पर बल से उपभोक्ता वस्तुओं की कमी तथा बढ़ता <b>खाद्य व विदेशी मुद्रा संकट</b> उत्पन्न हुआ, जिसने तीसरी योजना की दिशा तय की।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000074231","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A right prism has base perimeter 18 cm and height 5 cm. Lateral surface area? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक लंब प्रिज्म के आधार का परिमाप 18 cm और ऊँचाई 5 cm है। पार्श्व पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"80 cm²"},"2":{"en":"85 cm²"},"3":{"en":"90 cm²"},"4":{"en":"95 cm²"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"175\" height=\"145\" viewBox=\"0 0 175 145\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M20 45H100V120H20ZM20 45L50 20H130L100 45M130 20V95L100 120\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M50 20V95H130M50 95L20 120\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"138\" y=\"72\">h = 5</text></g></svg><br>LSA = Base perimeter × Height<br>\\(= 18 \\times 5 = \\boxed{90}\\) cm²<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 90 cm².</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"175\" height=\"145\" viewBox=\"0 0 175 145\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M20 45H100V120H20ZM20 45L50 20H130L100 45M130 20V95L100 120\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M50 20V95H130M50 95L20 120\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"138\" y=\"72\">h = 5</text></g></svg><br>पार्श्व पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल = आधार का परिमाप × ऊँचाई<br>\\(= 18 \\times 5 = \\boxed{90}\\) cm²<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 90 cm² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000074232","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"In a triangle, two sides measure 17 cm and 10 cm, and the included angle is 30°. Find the area of the triangle. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक त्रिभुज में, दो भुजाएँ 17 cm और 10 cm हैं, और उनके बीच का कोण 30° है। त्रिभुज का क्षेत्रफल ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"55.5 cm²"},"2":{"en":"44.5 cm²"},"3":{"en":"42.5 cm²"},"4":{"en":"32.5 cm²"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"206\" height=\"83\" viewBox=\"0 0 206 83\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M99 18L30 58H166Z\"/><path d=\"M52 58A22 22 0 0 0 49 47\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"99\" y=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"62\">B</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"62\">C</text><text x=\"98\" y=\"74\" text-anchor=\"middle\">17</text><text x=\"139\" y=\"38\"></text><text x=\"59\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"end\">10</text><text x=\"56\" y=\"54\">30°</text></g></svg><br>Area = \\(\\frac{1}{2}ab\\sin C\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 17 \\times 10 \\times \\frac{1}{2}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{42.5}\\) cm²<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 42.5 cm².</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"206\" height=\"83\" viewBox=\"0 0 206 83\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M99 18L30 58H166Z\"/><path d=\"M52 58A22 22 0 0 0 49 47\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"99\" y=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"62\">B</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"62\">C</text><text x=\"98\" y=\"74\" text-anchor=\"middle\">17</text><text x=\"139\" y=\"38\"></text><text x=\"59\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"end\">10</text><text x=\"56\" y=\"54\">30°</text></g></svg><br>क्षेत्रफल = \\(\\frac{1}{2}ab\\sin C\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 17 \\times 10 \\times \\frac{1}{2}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{42.5}\\) cm²<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 42.5 cm² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000074233","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"Given a cylinder with a diameter of 14 cm (so radius = 7 cm) and a height of 5 cm, what is its total surface area? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"14 cm व्यास (अर्थात त्रिज्या = 7 cm) और 5 cm ऊँचाई वाले एक बेलन का संपूर्ण पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल क्या है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"748 cm²"},"2":{"en":"528 cm²"},"3":{"en":"616 cm²"},"4":{"en":"572 cm²"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"170\" height=\"140\" viewBox=\"0 0 170 140\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><ellipse cx=\"70\" cy=\"22\" rx=\"50\" ry=\"12\"/><path d=\"M20 22V112M120 22V112M20 112a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 112a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M70 22H120M70 22V112\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"31\">7</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"72\">5</text></g></svg><br>TSA = \\(2\\pi r(r + h)\\)<br>\\(= 2 \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 7 \\times 12 = \\boxed{528}\\) cm²<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 528 cm².</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"170\" height=\"140\" viewBox=\"0 0 170 140\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><ellipse cx=\"70\" cy=\"22\" rx=\"50\" ry=\"12\"/><path d=\"M20 22V112M120 22V112M20 112a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 112a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M70 22H120M70 22V112\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"31\">7</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"72\">5</text></g></svg><br>संपूर्ण पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल = \\(2\\pi r(r + h)\\)<br>\\(= 2 \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 7 \\times 12 = \\boxed{528}\\) cm²<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 528 cm² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000074234","section":"MATH","topic":"Partnership","question":{"en":"Business partners A and B have made an initial investment of ₹4,000 and ₹5,000, respectively. A increased his investment after four months by ₹1,000, while B decreased his investment after four months by ₹1,000. C joined after another four months with ₹6,000. Determine the ratio of profits to be shared amongst A, B, and C at the end of the year. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"व्यावसायिक साझेदार A और B ने क्रमशः ₹4,000 और ₹5,000 का प्रारंभिक निवेश किया। चार महीने बाद A ने अपना निवेश ₹1,000 बढ़ा दिया, जबकि B ने चार महीने बाद अपना निवेश ₹1,000 घटा दिया। अगले चार महीने बाद C ₹6,000 के साथ जुड़ा। वर्ष के अंत में A, B और C के बीच बाँटे जाने वाले लाभ का अनुपात ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"14 : 13 : 12"},"2":{"en":"12 : 11 : 2"},"3":{"en":"14 : 13 : 6"},"4":{"en":"11 : 12 : 6"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"A = \\(4000 \\times 4 + 5000 \\times 8 = 56000\\)<br>B = \\(5000 \\times 4 + 4000 \\times 8 = 52000\\)<br>C = \\(6000 \\times 4 = 24000\\)<br>A : B : C = 56 : 52 : 24 = \\(\\boxed{14 : 13 : 6}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 14 : 13 : 6.</b>","hi":"A = \\(4000 \\times 4 + 5000 \\times 8 = 56000\\)<br>B = \\(5000 \\times 4 + 4000 \\times 8 = 52000\\)<br>C = \\(6000 \\times 4 = 24000\\)<br>A : B : C = 56 : 52 : 24 = \\(\\boxed{14 : 13 : 6}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 14 : 13 : 6 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000074235","section":"MATH","topic":"Compound Interest (CI)","question":{"en":"Find the compound interest on ₹20,000 at 15% per annum for 2 years 4 months, compounded annually. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"₹20,000 पर 15% वार्षिक दर से 2 वर्ष 4 महीने का चक्रवृद्धि ब्याज ज्ञात कीजिए, जब ब्याज वार्षिक रूप से संयोजित होता है। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹8072.50"},"2":{"en":"₹7772.50"},"3":{"en":"₹8772.50"},"4":{"en":"₹7072.50"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"2 years: \\(20000 \\times 1.15 \\times 1.15 = 26450\\)<br>4 months = \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\) year → rate = 5%: \\(26450 \\times 1.05 = 27772.50\\)<br>CI = \\(27772.50 - 20000 = \\boxed{7772.50}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): ₹7772.50.</b>","hi":"2 वर्ष: \\(20000 \\times 1.15 \\times 1.15 = 26450\\)<br>4 महीने = \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\) वर्ष → दर = 5%: \\(26450 \\times 1.05 = 27772.50\\)<br>चक्रवृद्धि ब्याज = \\(27772.50 - 20000 = \\boxed{7772.50}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): ₹7772.50 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000074236","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"A circle having a radius of 7 cm. A regular hexagon is drawn inside it. Find the area of the hexagon. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक वृत्त की त्रिज्या 7 cm है। इसके अंदर एक सम षट्भुज बनाया गया है। षट्भुज का क्षेत्रफल ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{162\\sqrt{3}}{12}\\) cm²"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{117\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\) cm²"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{157\\sqrt{13}}{2}\\) cm²"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{147\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\) cm²"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"150\" height=\"145\" viewBox=\"0 0 150 145\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><circle cx=\"75\" cy=\"72\" r=\"55\"/><path d=\"M130 72L102 24L48 24L20 72L47 120L102 120Z\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M75 72H130M75 72L102 24\"/><circle cx=\"75\" cy=\"72\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"102\" y=\"86\" text-anchor=\"middle\">7</text><text x=\"115\" y=\"42\">7</text><text x=\"69\" y=\"86\">O</text></g></svg><br>Side of hexagon = radius = 7 cm<br>Area = \\(6 \\times \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\times 7^2\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{147\\sqrt{3}}{2}}\\) cm²<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): \\(\\frac{147\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\) cm².</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"150\" height=\"145\" viewBox=\"0 0 150 145\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><circle cx=\"75\" cy=\"72\" r=\"55\"/><path d=\"M130 72L102 24L48 24L20 72L47 120L102 120Z\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M75 72H130M75 72L102 24\"/><circle cx=\"75\" cy=\"72\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"102\" y=\"86\" text-anchor=\"middle\">7</text><text x=\"115\" y=\"42\">7</text><text x=\"69\" y=\"86\">O</text></g></svg><br>षट्भुज की भुजा = त्रिज्या = 7 cm<br>क्षेत्रफल = \\(6 \\times \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\times 7^2\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{147\\sqrt{3}}{2}}\\) cm²<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): \\(\\frac{147\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\) cm² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000074237","section":"MATH","topic":"Average","question":{"en":"The average of 7 numbers is 30. If the average of the first three numbers is 25 and the average of the last three numbers is 35, what is the value of the fourth number? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"7 संख्याओं का औसत 30 है। यदि पहली तीन संख्याओं का औसत 25 और अंतिम तीन संख्याओं का औसत 35 है, तो चौथी संख्या का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"40"},"2":{"en":"30"},"3":{"en":"50"},"4":{"en":"60"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Total = \\(7 \\times 30 = 210\\)<br>First three = 75, last three = 105<br>Fourth = \\(210 - 75 - 105 = \\boxed{30}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 30.</b>","hi":"कुल = \\(7 \\times 30 = 210\\)<br>पहली तीन = 75, अंतिम तीन = 105<br>चौथी = \\(210 - 75 - 105 = \\boxed{30}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 30 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000074238","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"The diameter of a circular wheel is 84 cm. How far (in meters) will it travel in 100 revolutions? (Take \\(\\pi = \\frac{22}{7}\\)) [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक वृत्ताकार पहिये का व्यास 84 cm है। 100 चक्करों में यह कितनी दूरी (मीटर में) तय करेगा? (\\(\\pi = \\frac{22}{7}\\) लीजिए) [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"234 m"},"2":{"en":"264 m"},"3":{"en":"214 m"},"4":{"en":"254 m"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"130\" height=\"130\" viewBox=\"0 0 130 130\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><circle cx=\"65\" cy=\"65\" r=\"50\"/><circle cx=\"65\" cy=\"65\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#000\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M65 65H115\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"60\">42</text></g></svg><br>Distance in 1 revolution = \\(\\pi d = \\frac{22}{7} \\times 84 = 264\\) cm<br>100 revolutions = 26400 cm = \\(\\boxed{264}\\) m<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 264 m.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"130\" height=\"130\" viewBox=\"0 0 130 130\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><circle cx=\"65\" cy=\"65\" r=\"50\"/><circle cx=\"65\" cy=\"65\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#000\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M65 65H115\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"60\">42</text></g></svg><br>1 चक्कर में दूरी = \\(\\pi d = \\frac{22}{7} \\times 84 = 264\\) cm<br>100 चक्कर = 26400 cm = \\(\\boxed{264}\\) m<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 264 m है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000074239","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A cone has height 8 cm and volume 96π cm³. Find its curved surface area. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक शंकु की ऊँचाई 8 cm और आयतन 96π cm³ है। इसका वक्र पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"60π cm²"},"2":{"en":"55π cm²"},"3":{"en":"65π cm²"},"4":{"en":"70π cm²"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"170\" height=\"135\" viewBox=\"0 0 170 135\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M70 15L20 110M70 15L120 110M20 110a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 110a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M70 15V110M70 110H120\"/><path d=\"M70 100h8v10\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"96\" y=\"106\">r</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"72\">8</text><text x=\"102\" y=\"56\">l</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\pi r^2 \\times 8 = 96\\pi \\Rightarrow r^2 = 36 \\Rightarrow r = 6\\)<br>\\(l = \\sqrt{6^2 + 8^2} = 10\\)<br>CSA = \\(\\pi r l = \\pi \\times 6 \\times 10 = \\boxed{60\\pi}\\) cm²<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 60π cm².</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"170\" height=\"135\" viewBox=\"0 0 170 135\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M70 15L20 110M70 15L120 110M20 110a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 110a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M70 15V110M70 110H120\"/><path d=\"M70 100h8v10\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"96\" y=\"106\">r</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"72\">8</text><text x=\"102\" y=\"56\">l</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\pi r^2 \\times 8 = 96\\pi \\Rightarrow r^2 = 36 \\Rightarrow r = 6\\)<br>\\(l = \\sqrt{6^2 + 8^2} = 10\\)<br>वक्र पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल = \\(\\pi r l = \\pi \\times 6 \\times 10 = \\boxed{60\\pi}\\) cm²<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 60π cm² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000074240","section":"MATH","topic":"Height and Distance","question":{"en":"From a point exactly midway between two towers A and B, the angles of elevation of their tops are 45° and 60° respectively. Find the ratio of the height of A to that of B. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दो मीनारों A और B के ठीक मध्य स्थित एक बिंदु से उनके शीर्षों के उन्नयन कोण क्रमशः 45° और 60° हैं। A की ऊँचाई और B की ऊँचाई का अनुपात ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{3} : 1\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(2 : \\sqrt{3}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{3} : 2\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(1 : \\sqrt{3}\\)"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"235\" height=\"175\" viewBox=\"0 0 235 175\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M40 74V154H200V15M40 74L120 154L200 15\"/><path d=\"M102 154A18 18 0 0 1 107 141\"/><path d=\"M138 154A18 18 0 0 0 129 138\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"35\" y=\"78\" text-anchor=\"end\">A</text><text x=\"205\" y=\"19\">B</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"middle\">P</text><text x=\"35\" y=\"118\" text-anchor=\"end\">h₁</text><text x=\"205\" y=\"88\">h₂</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"middle\">d</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"middle\">d</text><text x=\"98\" y=\"149\" text-anchor=\"end\">45°</text><text x=\"142\" y=\"149\">60°</text></g></svg><br>Distance from P to each tower = d<br>\\(h_1 = d\\tan 45^\\circ = d,\\ h_2 = d\\tan 60^\\circ = \\sqrt{3}d\\)<br>\\(h_1 : h_2 = \\boxed{1 : \\sqrt{3}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): \\(1 : \\sqrt{3}\\).</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"235\" height=\"175\" viewBox=\"0 0 235 175\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M40 74V154H200V15M40 74L120 154L200 15\"/><path d=\"M102 154A18 18 0 0 1 107 141\"/><path d=\"M138 154A18 18 0 0 0 129 138\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"35\" y=\"78\" text-anchor=\"end\">A</text><text x=\"205\" y=\"19\">B</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"middle\">P</text><text x=\"35\" y=\"118\" text-anchor=\"end\">h₁</text><text x=\"205\" y=\"88\">h₂</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"middle\">d</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"middle\">d</text><text x=\"98\" y=\"149\" text-anchor=\"end\">45°</text><text x=\"142\" y=\"149\">60°</text></g></svg><br>P से प्रत्येक मीनार की दूरी = d<br>\\(h_1 = d\\tan 45^\\circ = d,\\ h_2 = d\\tan 60^\\circ = \\sqrt{3}d\\)<br>\\(h_1 : h_2 = \\boxed{1 : \\sqrt{3}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): \\(1 : \\sqrt{3}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000074241","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"AB is a chord in a circle with center O, and C is a point on the minor arc AB between A and B. Tangents drawn at points A and B meet at point D. If \\(\\angle ACB = 116^\\circ\\), find \\(\\angle ADB\\). [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"केंद्र O वाले एक वृत्त में AB एक जीवा है, और C, A और B के बीच लघु चाप AB पर एक बिंदु है। बिंदुओं A और B पर खींची गई स्पर्श रेखाएँ बिंदु D पर मिलती हैं। यदि \\(\\angle ACB = 116^\\circ\\) है, तो \\(\\angle ADB\\) ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"65°"},"2":{"en":"48°"},"3":{"en":"52°"},"4":{"en":"74°"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"179\" height=\"242\" viewBox=\"0 0 179 242\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M34 121L89 26L144 121M40 124L43 119L37 116M139 124L136 119L141 116M34 121L89 89L144 121M81 94A10 10 0 0 0 98 94M83 36A12 12 0 0 0 95 36\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M89 153L34 121M89 153L144 121\"/><circle cx=\"89\" cy=\"153\" r=\"63\"/><circle cx=\"89\" cy=\"153\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"89\" y=\"169\">O</text><text x=\"21\" y=\"118\">A</text><text x=\"158\" y=\"118\">B</text><text x=\"89\" y=\"23\">D</text><text x=\"89\" y=\"86\">C</text><text x=\"89\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"11\">116°</text><text x=\"89\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"11\">?</text></g></svg><br>C is on the minor arc → major arc AB = \\(2 \\times 116^\\circ = 232^\\circ\\)<br>Minor arc AB = \\(360^\\circ - 232^\\circ = 128^\\circ\\)<br>\\(\\angle ADB = 180^\\circ - 128^\\circ = \\boxed{52^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 52°.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"179\" height=\"242\" viewBox=\"0 0 179 242\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M34 121L89 26L144 121M40 124L43 119L37 116M139 124L136 119L141 116M34 121L89 89L144 121M81 94A10 10 0 0 0 98 94M83 36A12 12 0 0 0 95 36\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M89 153L34 121M89 153L144 121\"/><circle cx=\"89\" cy=\"153\" r=\"63\"/><circle cx=\"89\" cy=\"153\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"89\" y=\"169\">O</text><text x=\"21\" y=\"118\">A</text><text x=\"158\" y=\"118\">B</text><text x=\"89\" y=\"23\">D</text><text x=\"89\" y=\"86\">C</text><text x=\"89\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"11\">116°</text><text x=\"89\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"11\">?</text></g></svg><br>C लघु चाप पर है → दीर्घ चाप AB = \\(2 \\times 116^\\circ = 232^\\circ\\)<br>लघु चाप AB = \\(360^\\circ - 232^\\circ = 128^\\circ\\)<br>\\(\\angle ADB = 180^\\circ - 128^\\circ = \\boxed{52^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 52° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000074242","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If \\(\\sqrt{13}\\sin\\theta = 2\\), find the value of \\(\\frac{3\\tan\\theta + \\sqrt{13}\\sin\\theta}{\\sqrt{13}\\cos\\theta - 3\\tan\\theta}\\). [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि \\(\\sqrt{13}\\sin\\theta = 2\\) है, तो \\(\\frac{3\\tan\\theta + \\sqrt{13}\\sin\\theta}{\\sqrt{13}\\cos\\theta - 3\\tan\\theta}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"6"},"2":{"en":"4"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"2"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\sin\\theta = \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\Rightarrow \\cos\\theta = \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}},\\ \\tan\\theta = \\frac{2}{3}\\)<br>Numerator = \\(3 \\times \\frac{2}{3} + 2 = 4\\); Denominator = \\(3 - 3 \\times \\frac{2}{3} = 1\\)<br>Value = \\(\\boxed{4}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 4.</b>","hi":"\\(\\sin\\theta = \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\Rightarrow \\cos\\theta = \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}},\\ \\tan\\theta = \\frac{2}{3}\\)<br>अंश = \\(3 \\times \\frac{2}{3} + 2 = 4\\); हर = \\(3 - 3 \\times \\frac{2}{3} = 1\\)<br>मान = \\(\\boxed{4}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 4 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000074243","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A spherical iron ball of radius 9 cm is melted and recast into a cone of base radius 6 cm. What is the height of the cone? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"9 cm त्रिज्या वाली लोहे की एक गोलाकार गेंद को पिघलाकर 6 cm आधार त्रिज्या वाले एक शंकु में ढाला जाता है। शंकु की ऊँचाई क्या है? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"78 cm"},"2":{"en":"81 cm"},"3":{"en":"86 cm"},"4":{"en":"92 cm"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"135\" height=\"125\" viewBox=\"0 0 135 125\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><circle cx=\"65\" cy=\"65\" r=\"50\"/><path d=\"M15 65a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M15 65a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M65 65H115\"/><circle cx=\"65\" cy=\"65\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"61\">9</text></g></svg>&nbsp; <svg width=\"170\" height=\"135\" viewBox=\"0 0 170 135\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M70 15L20 110M70 15L120 110M20 110a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 110a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M70 15V110M70 110H120\"/><path d=\"M70 100h8v10\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"96\" y=\"106\">6</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"72\">h</text><text x=\"102\" y=\"56\">l</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\frac{4}{3}\\pi (9)^3 = \\frac{1}{3}\\pi (6)^2 h\\)<br>\\(4 \\times 729 = 36h\\)<br>\\(h = \\boxed{81}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 81 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"135\" height=\"125\" viewBox=\"0 0 135 125\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><circle cx=\"65\" cy=\"65\" r=\"50\"/><path d=\"M15 65a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M15 65a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M65 65H115\"/><circle cx=\"65\" cy=\"65\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"61\">9</text></g></svg>&nbsp; <svg width=\"170\" height=\"135\" viewBox=\"0 0 170 135\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M70 15L20 110M70 15L120 110M20 110a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 110a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M70 15V110M70 110H120\"/><path d=\"M70 100h8v10\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"96\" y=\"106\">6</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"72\">h</text><text x=\"102\" y=\"56\">l</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\frac{4}{3}\\pi (9)^3 = \\frac{1}{3}\\pi (6)^2 h\\)<br>\\(4 \\times 729 = 36h\\)<br>\\(h = \\boxed{81}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 81 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000074244","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In triangle ABC, DE is parallel to BC, AD = x + 2, DB = 3x, AE = 4x + 1, EC = 7x. Find the value of x (x &gt; 0). [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"त्रिभुज ABC में, DE, BC के समांतर है, AD = x + 2, DB = 3x, AE = 4x + 1, EC = 7x है। x का मान ज्ञात कीजिए (x &gt; 0)। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{17}{5}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{11}{5}\\)"},"4":{"en":"5"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"290\" height=\"170\" viewBox=\"0 0 290 170\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M120 18L40 150H210ZM88 71L156 71\"/><path d=\"M119 67l5 4-5 4M122 146l5 4-5 4\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"120\" y=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"154\">B</text><text x=\"214\" y=\"154\">C</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"75\">D</text><text x=\"161\" y=\"75\">E</text><text x=\"97\" y=\"48\" text-anchor=\"end\">x + 2</text><text x=\"57\" y=\"114\" text-anchor=\"end\">3x</text><text x=\"145\" y=\"48\">4x + 1</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"114\">7x</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\frac{AD}{DB} = \\frac{AE}{EC} \\Rightarrow \\frac{x + 2}{3x} = \\frac{4x + 1}{7x}\\)<br>\\(7(x + 2) = 3(4x + 1) \\Rightarrow 7x + 14 = 12x + 3\\)<br>\\(x = \\boxed{\\frac{11}{5}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): \\(\\frac{11}{5}\\).</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"290\" height=\"170\" viewBox=\"0 0 290 170\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M120 18L40 150H210ZM88 71L156 71\"/><path d=\"M119 67l5 4-5 4M122 146l5 4-5 4\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"120\" y=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"154\">B</text><text x=\"214\" y=\"154\">C</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"75\">D</text><text x=\"161\" y=\"75\">E</text><text x=\"97\" y=\"48\" text-anchor=\"end\">x + 2</text><text x=\"57\" y=\"114\" text-anchor=\"end\">3x</text><text x=\"145\" y=\"48\">4x + 1</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"114\">7x</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\frac{AD}{DB} = \\frac{AE}{EC} \\Rightarrow \\frac{x + 2}{3x} = \\frac{4x + 1}{7x}\\)<br>\\(7(x + 2) = 3(4x + 1) \\Rightarrow 7x + 14 = 12x + 3\\)<br>\\(x = \\boxed{\\frac{11}{5}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): \\(\\frac{11}{5}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000074245","section":"MATH","topic":"Mixture and Alligation","question":{"en":"A container holds a mixture of milk and water in the ratio 7:5. A worker draws off 24 liters of this mixture and refills the container with 24 liters of a pre-mixed blend of milk and water in a 1:1 ratio. If the final ratio of milk to water in the container becomes 17:13, what was the initial volume of the mixture (in liters.)? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक पात्र में दूध और पानी का मिश्रण 7:5 के अनुपात में है। एक कर्मचारी इस मिश्रण का 24 लीटर निकालता है और पात्र को 1:1 अनुपात वाले दूध और पानी के 24 लीटर पूर्व-मिश्रित मिश्रण से फिर भर देता है। यदि पात्र में दूध और पानी का अंतिम अनुपात 17:13 हो जाता है, तो मिश्रण का प्रारंभिक आयतन (लीटर में) क्या था? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"108"},"2":{"en":"120"},"3":{"en":"144"},"4":{"en":"180"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Let initial volume = V. After removing 24 L, milk = \\(\\frac{7}{12}(V - 24)\\), water = \\(\\frac{5}{12}(V - 24)\\); then 12 L of each is added<br>\\(\\frac{7(V - 24) + 144}{5(V - 24) + 144} = \\frac{17}{13}\\)<br>\\(91(V - 24) + 1872 = 85(V - 24) + 2448 \\Rightarrow 6(V - 24) = 576\\)<br>\\(V - 24 = 96 \\Rightarrow V = \\boxed{120}\\) L<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 120.</b>","hi":"माना प्रारंभिक आयतन = V. 24 L निकालने पर दूध = \\(\\frac{7}{12}(V - 24)\\), पानी = \\(\\frac{5}{12}(V - 24)\\); फिर प्रत्येक का 12 L मिलाया जाता है<br>\\(\\frac{7(V - 24) + 144}{5(V - 24) + 144} = \\frac{17}{13}\\)<br>\\(91(V - 24) + 1872 = 85(V - 24) + 2448 \\Rightarrow 6(V - 24) = 576\\)<br>\\(V - 24 = 96 \\Rightarrow V = \\boxed{120}\\) L<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 120 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000074246","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"X is 50% more efficient than Y, Z takes twice as much time as X and Y working together to complete a job. X, Y and Z start working together but after 4 days, Z leaves. The remaining work is completed by X and Y. If X alone can complete the entire job in 20 days, determine the total time taken to complete the work in the given scenario. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"X, Y से 50% अधिक कुशल है, Z किसी कार्य को पूरा करने में X और Y द्वारा मिलकर लिए गए समय का दोगुना समय लेता है। X, Y और Z एक साथ कार्य शुरू करते हैं लेकिन 4 दिन बाद Z चला जाता है। शेष कार्य X और Y पूरा करते हैं। यदि X अकेले पूरा कार्य 20 दिनों में कर सकता है, तो दी गई स्थिति में कार्य पूरा करने में लगा कुल समय ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"10 days","hi":"10 दिन"},"2":{"en":"12 days","hi":"12 दिन"},"3":{"en":"15 days","hi":"15 दिन"},"4":{"en":"18 days","hi":"18 दिन"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Efficiency X : Y = 3 : 2; Z = \\(\\frac{3 + 2}{2} = 2.5\\)<br>Work = \\(20 \\times 3 = 60\\) units<br>4 days by all: \\(7.5 \\times 4 = 30\\) units; remaining 30 by X + Y (5/day) = 6 days<br>Total = 4 + 6 = \\(\\boxed{10}\\) days<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 10 days.</b>","hi":"दक्षता X : Y = 3 : 2; Z = \\(\\frac{3 + 2}{2} = 2.5\\)<br>कार्य = \\(20 \\times 3 = 60\\) इकाई<br>सभी द्वारा 4 दिन: \\(7.5 \\times 4 = 30\\) इकाई; शेष 30, X + Y (5/दिन) द्वारा = 6 दिन<br>कुल = 4 + 6 = \\(\\boxed{10}\\) दिन<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 10 दिन है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000074247","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"Solve for acute \\(\\theta\\): \\(\\cos 3\\theta = \\sin 2\\theta\\) [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"न्यून कोण \\(\\theta\\) के लिए हल कीजिए: \\(\\cos 3\\theta = \\sin 2\\theta\\) [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"45°"},"2":{"en":"30°"},"3":{"en":"22.5°"},"4":{"en":"18°"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(\\cos 3\\theta = \\sin 2\\theta \\Rightarrow 3\\theta + 2\\theta = 90^\\circ\\)<br>\\(5\\theta = 90^\\circ\\)<br>\\(\\theta = \\boxed{18^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 18°.</b>","hi":"\\(\\cos 3\\theta = \\sin 2\\theta \\Rightarrow 3\\theta + 2\\theta = 90^\\circ\\)<br>\\(5\\theta = 90^\\circ\\)<br>\\(\\theta = \\boxed{18^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 18° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000074248","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"Evaluate: \\(\\cos^2 10^\\circ + \\cos^2 20^\\circ + \\cos^2 30^\\circ + \\cos^2 40^\\circ + \\cos^2 50^\\circ + \\cos^2 60^\\circ + \\cos^2 70^\\circ + \\cos^2 80^\\circ\\) [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"मान ज्ञात कीजिए: \\(\\cos^2 10^\\circ + \\cos^2 20^\\circ + \\cos^2 30^\\circ + \\cos^2 40^\\circ + \\cos^2 50^\\circ + \\cos^2 60^\\circ + \\cos^2 70^\\circ + \\cos^2 80^\\circ\\) [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3"},"2":{"en":"4"},"3":{"en":"5"},"4":{"en":"2"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\cos^2 80^\\circ = \\sin^2 10^\\circ\\), so \\(\\cos^2 10^\\circ + \\cos^2 80^\\circ = 1\\)<br>Pairs (10°, 80°), (20°, 70°), (30°, 60°), (40°, 50°) each give 1<br>Sum = \\(\\boxed{4}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 4.</b>","hi":"\\(\\cos^2 80^\\circ = \\sin^2 10^\\circ\\), अतः \\(\\cos^2 10^\\circ + \\cos^2 80^\\circ = 1\\)<br>युग्म (10°, 80°), (20°, 70°), (30°, 60°), (40°, 50°) प्रत्येक का योग 1<br>योग = \\(\\boxed{4}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 4 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000074249","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Evaluate the following expression without direct calculation by using an appropriate algebraic identity:<br>\\(\\frac{(3.75)^2 - (1.25)^2}{(3.75)^2 + 2(3.75)(1.25) + (1.25)^2}\\) [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"उपयुक्त बीजीय सर्वसमिका का उपयोग करके, सीधे गणना किए बिना निम्नलिखित व्यंजक का मान ज्ञात कीजिए:<br>\\(\\frac{(3.75)^2 - (1.25)^2}{(3.75)^2 + 2(3.75)(1.25) + (1.25)^2}\\) [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{4}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{5}\\)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{a^2 - b^2}{(a + b)^2} = \\frac{a - b}{a + b}\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{3.75 - 1.25}{3.75 + 1.25} = \\frac{2.5}{5}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{1}{2}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{a^2 - b^2}{(a + b)^2} = \\frac{a - b}{a + b}\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{3.75 - 1.25}{3.75 + 1.25} = \\frac{2.5}{5}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{1}{2}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000074250","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If m − n = 15 and mn = 26, find the value of (m + n)². [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि m − n = 15 और mn = 26 है, तो (m + n)² का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"229"},"2":{"en":"119"},"3":{"en":"239"},"4":{"en":"329"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\((m + n)^2 = (m - n)^2 + 4mn\\)<br>\\(= 225 + 104 = \\boxed{329}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 329.</b>","hi":"\\((m + n)^2 = (m - n)^2 + 4mn\\)<br>\\(= 225 + 104 = \\boxed{329}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 329 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000074251","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Simplify the following expression completely:<br>\\((2\\sqrt{3} - \\sqrt{2})(2\\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{2})\\) [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित व्यंजक को पूर्ण रूप से सरल कीजिए:<br>\\((2\\sqrt{3} - \\sqrt{2})(2\\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{2})\\) [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"14"},"2":{"en":"10"},"3":{"en":"12"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\((a - b)(a + b) = a^2 - b^2\\)<br>\\(= (2\\sqrt{3})^2 - (\\sqrt{2})^2 = 12 - 2 = \\boxed{10}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 10.</b>","hi":"\\((a - b)(a + b) = a^2 - b^2\\)<br>\\(= (2\\sqrt{3})^2 - (\\sqrt{2})^2 = 12 - 2 = \\boxed{10}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 10 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000074252","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Simplify the following expression completely:<br>\\(\\frac{\\sqrt{10 + \\sqrt{84}} + \\sqrt{10 - \\sqrt{84}}}{\\sqrt{14 + \\sqrt{96}} - \\sqrt{14 - \\sqrt{96}}}\\) [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित व्यंजक को पूर्ण रूप से सरल कीजिए:<br>\\(\\frac{\\sqrt{10 + \\sqrt{84}} + \\sqrt{10 - \\sqrt{84}}}{\\sqrt{14 + \\sqrt{96}} - \\sqrt{14 - \\sqrt{96}}}\\) [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{2}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{2}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{3}}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{7}{3}\\right)}\\)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(10 \\pm \\sqrt{84} = 10 \\pm 2\\sqrt{21} = (\\sqrt{7} \\pm \\sqrt{3})^2\\) → numerator = \\(2\\sqrt{7}\\)<br>\\(14 \\pm \\sqrt{96} = 14 \\pm 2\\sqrt{24} = (\\sqrt{12} \\pm \\sqrt{2})^2\\) → denominator = \\(2\\sqrt{2}\\)<br>Value = \\(\\frac{2\\sqrt{7}}{2\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{2}} = \\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{2}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{2}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(10 \\pm \\sqrt{84} = 10 \\pm 2\\sqrt{21} = (\\sqrt{7} \\pm \\sqrt{3})^2\\) → अंश = \\(2\\sqrt{7}\\)<br>\\(14 \\pm \\sqrt{96} = 14 \\pm 2\\sqrt{24} = (\\sqrt{12} \\pm \\sqrt{2})^2\\) → हर = \\(2\\sqrt{2}\\)<br>मान = \\(\\frac{2\\sqrt{7}}{2\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{2}} = \\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{2}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{2}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000074253","section":"MATH","topic":"Mixture and Alligation","question":{"en":"A trader mixes two grades of dry fruits costing ₹600 per kg and ₹900 per kg, respectively. The resulting mixture is sold at ₹1000 per kg, yielding a profit of 25%. If the quantity of the costlier grade exceeds the quantity of the cheaper grade by 12 kg, find the total quantity of the mixture. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक व्यापारी क्रमशः ₹600 प्रति kg और ₹900 प्रति kg मूल्य वाले सूखे मेवों की दो किस्मों को मिलाता है। परिणामी मिश्रण ₹1000 प्रति kg पर बेचा जाता है, जिससे 25% लाभ होता है। यदि महँगी किस्म की मात्रा सस्ती किस्म की मात्रा से 12 kg अधिक है, तो मिश्रण की कुल मात्रा ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"18 kg"},"2":{"en":"24 kg"},"3":{"en":"36 kg"},"4":{"en":"48 kg"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"CP of mixture = \\(\\frac{1000}{125} \\times 100 = 800\\) per kg<br>Alligation: Cheap : Costly = (900 − 800) : (800 − 600) = 1 : 2<br>Difference = 1 part = 12 kg<br>Total = 3 parts = \\(\\boxed{36}\\) kg<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 36 kg.</b>","hi":"मिश्रण का क्रय मूल्य = \\(\\frac{1000}{125} \\times 100 = 800\\) प्रति kg<br>एलीगेशन: सस्ती : महँगी = (900 − 800) : (800 − 600) = 1 : 2<br>अंतर = 1 भाग = 12 kg<br>कुल = 3 भाग = \\(\\boxed{36}\\) kg<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 36 kg है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000074254","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"If a straight line acts as a common tangent to two different circles, the perpendicular distance from the center of each circle to this line is equal to [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि एक सरल रेखा दो भिन्न वृत्तों की उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखा है, तो प्रत्येक वृत्त के केंद्र से इस रेखा की लंबवत दूरी बराबर होती है [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"the radius of the respective circle","hi":"संबंधित वृत्त की त्रिज्या के"},"2":{"en":"the sum of the radii","hi":"त्रिज्याओं के योग के"},"3":{"en":"the difference of the radii","hi":"त्रिज्याओं के अंतर के"},"4":{"en":"half the sum of the radii","hi":"त्रिज्याओं के योग के आधे के"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"A tangent is perpendicular to the radius at the point of contact.<br>So the perpendicular distance from each centre to the tangent line equals that circle's radius.<br>\\(\\boxed{\\text{Radius of the respective circle}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): the radius of the respective circle.</b>","hi":"स्पर्श बिंदु पर स्पर्श रेखा त्रिज्या पर लंब होती है।<br>अतः प्रत्येक केंद्र से स्पर्श रेखा की लंबवत दूरी उस वृत्त की त्रिज्या के बराबर होती है।<br>\\(\\boxed{\\text{Radius of the respective circle}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): संबंधित वृत्त की त्रिज्या के है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000074255","section":"MATH","topic":"Percentage","question":{"en":"A test has 90 questions: 10 numerical, 35 reasoning and 45 general-awareness questions. A candidate answers 80%, 60% and 60% of the respective sections correctly. With no negative marking, at least 70% of all questions must be correct to qualify. What is the minimum number of additional wrong answers that must be corrected? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक परीक्षा में 90 प्रश्न हैं: 10 संख्यात्मक, 35 तर्कशक्ति और 45 सामान्य जागरूकता के प्रश्न। एक अभ्यर्थी संबंधित खंडों के क्रमशः 80%, 60% और 60% प्रश्न सही करता है। कोई ऋणात्मक अंकन नहीं है, और उत्तीर्ण होने के लिए सभी प्रश्नों में से कम से कम 70% सही होने चाहिए। न्यूनतम कितने अतिरिक्त गलत उत्तरों को सही करना होगा? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"7"},"2":{"en":"6"},"3":{"en":"8"},"4":{"en":"9"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Correct = 80% of 10 + 60% of 35 + 60% of 45 = 8 + 21 + 27 = 56<br>Required = 70% of 90 = 63<br>Additional = 63 − 56 = \\(\\boxed{7}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 7.</b>","hi":"सही = 10 का 80% + 35 का 60% + 45 का 60% = 8 + 21 + 27 = 56<br>आवश्यक = 90 का 70% = 63<br>अतिरिक्त = 63 − 56 = \\(\\boxed{7}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 7 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000074256","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the following question, a sentence with a blank is given, followed by five words labeled (1), (2), (3), (4), and (5). Choose the word that fills the blank appropriately in the context of the passage.<br><br>The rapid proliferation of artificial intelligence (AI) technologies (1)___ profound ethical quandaries, necessitating an urgent reevaluation of longstanding moral frameworks. While AI has demonstrably enhanced efficiency across industries, its deployment (2)___ contentious debates surrounding privacy, accountability, and autonomy. One critical concern is the opacity of algorithmic decision-making, wherein even developers may be unable to fully elucidate how outcomes are generated.<br><br>This phenomenon, often termed the “black box” problem, undermines (3)___ transparency, a principle integral to ethical governance. Moreover, AI systems trained on biased datasets risk perpetuating and even exacerbating systemic inequalities.<br><br>Compounding these challenges is the issue of agency: when machines perform autonomous actions, determining liability (4)___ complex and ambiguous. Beyond technical considerations, the ethical dilemmas posed by AI interrogate deeper philosophical questions about what it means to be human, to choose freely, and to coexist responsibly with non-human intelligences.<br><br>Thus, a multidisciplinary approach, encompassing philosophy, computer science, law, and sociology, is imperative to ensure that technological advancement remains (5)___ benign in its societal impact. Unless proactive governance mechanisms are implemented, humanity risks ceding essential elements of moral agency to entities whose operations it neither fully understands nor adequately controls.<br><br><br>Choose correct tense. (1) [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"have posed"},"2":{"en":"poses"},"3":{"en":"posed"},"4":{"en":"had posed"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: The singular head noun “proliferation” takes the singular verb “poses.”</b><br>The simple present states the general ethical consequence of rapid AI proliferation.<br>“Have posed” lacks subject–verb agreement; “posed” shifts to the past.<br>“Had posed” requires an earlier past reference point that the passage does not supply.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): poses.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000074257","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the following question, a sentence with a blank is given, followed by five words labeled (1), (2), (3), (4), and (5). Choose the word that fills the blank appropriately in the context of the passage.<br><br>The rapid proliferation of artificial intelligence (AI) technologies (1)___ profound ethical quandaries, necessitating an urgent reevaluation of longstanding moral frameworks. While AI has demonstrably enhanced efficiency across industries, its deployment (2)___ contentious debates surrounding privacy, accountability, and autonomy. One critical concern is the opacity of algorithmic decision-making, wherein even developers may be unable to fully elucidate how outcomes are generated.<br><br>This phenomenon, often termed the “black box” problem, undermines (3)___ transparency, a principle integral to ethical governance. Moreover, AI systems trained on biased datasets risk perpetuating and even exacerbating systemic inequalities.<br><br>Compounding these challenges is the issue of agency: when machines perform autonomous actions, determining liability (4)___ complex and ambiguous. Beyond technical considerations, the ethical dilemmas posed by AI interrogate deeper philosophical questions about what it means to be human, to choose freely, and to coexist responsibly with non-human intelligences.<br><br>Thus, a multidisciplinary approach, encompassing philosophy, computer science, law, and sociology, is imperative to ensure that technological advancement remains (5)___ benign in its societal impact. Unless proactive governance mechanisms are implemented, humanity risks ceding essential elements of moral agency to entities whose operations it neither fully understands nor adequately controls.<br><br><br>Choose correct subject-verb agreement. (2) [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"is sparking"},"2":{"en":"are sparking"},"3":{"en":"sparked"},"4":{"en":"sparking"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: The singular subject “deployment” takes “is sparking.”</b><br>Present continuous describes debates currently being generated by AI deployment.<br>“Are sparking” lacks agreement; “sparked” shifts to the past.<br>“Sparking” cannot serve as the finite verb here.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): is sparking.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000074258","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the following question, a sentence with a blank is given, followed by five words labeled (1), (2), (3), (4), and (5). Choose the word that fills the blank appropriately in the context of the passage.<br><br>The rapid proliferation of artificial intelligence (AI) technologies (1)___ profound ethical quandaries, necessitating an urgent reevaluation of longstanding moral frameworks. While AI has demonstrably enhanced efficiency across industries, its deployment (2)___ contentious debates surrounding privacy, accountability, and autonomy. One critical concern is the opacity of algorithmic decision-making, wherein even developers may be unable to fully elucidate how outcomes are generated.<br><br>This phenomenon, often termed the “black box” problem, undermines (3)___ transparency, a principle integral to ethical governance. Moreover, AI systems trained on biased datasets risk perpetuating and even exacerbating systemic inequalities.<br><br>Compounding these challenges is the issue of agency: when machines perform autonomous actions, determining liability (4)___ complex and ambiguous. Beyond technical considerations, the ethical dilemmas posed by AI interrogate deeper philosophical questions about what it means to be human, to choose freely, and to coexist responsibly with non-human intelligences.<br><br>Thus, a multidisciplinary approach, encompassing philosophy, computer science, law, and sociology, is imperative to ensure that technological advancement remains (5)___ benign in its societal impact. Unless proactive governance mechanisms are implemented, humanity risks ceding essential elements of moral agency to entities whose operations it neither fully understands nor adequately controls.<br><br><br>In this context, “transparency” most nearly refers to: (3) [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Maintaining secrecy"},"2":{"en":"Complete openness and clarity"},"3":{"en":"Computational complexity"},"4":{"en":"Unpredictable variability"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Transparency (पारदर्शिता) = openness and clarity about processes and decisions.</b><br>Black-box decision-making undermines the ability to understand algorithmic outcomes.<br>Maintaining secrecy is the opposite; computational complexity and variability do not define transparency.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Complete openness and clarity.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000074259","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the following question, a sentence with a blank is given, followed by five words labeled (1), (2), (3), (4), and (5). Choose the word that fills the blank appropriately in the context of the passage.<br><br>The rapid proliferation of artificial intelligence (AI) technologies (1)___ profound ethical quandaries, necessitating an urgent reevaluation of longstanding moral frameworks. While AI has demonstrably enhanced efficiency across industries, its deployment (2)___ contentious debates surrounding privacy, accountability, and autonomy. One critical concern is the opacity of algorithmic decision-making, wherein even developers may be unable to fully elucidate how outcomes are generated.<br><br>This phenomenon, often termed the “black box” problem, undermines (3)___ transparency, a principle integral to ethical governance. Moreover, AI systems trained on biased datasets risk perpetuating and even exacerbating systemic inequalities.<br><br>Compounding these challenges is the issue of agency: when machines perform autonomous actions, determining liability (4)___ complex and ambiguous. Beyond technical considerations, the ethical dilemmas posed by AI interrogate deeper philosophical questions about what it means to be human, to choose freely, and to coexist responsibly with non-human intelligences.<br><br>Thus, a multidisciplinary approach, encompassing philosophy, computer science, law, and sociology, is imperative to ensure that technological advancement remains (5)___ benign in its societal impact. Unless proactive governance mechanisms are implemented, humanity risks ceding essential elements of moral agency to entities whose operations it neither fully understands nor adequately controls.<br><br><br>Choose correct verb form. (4) [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"become"},"2":{"en":"becoming"},"3":{"en":"becomes"},"4":{"en":"has become"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Present perfect emphasizes the current result of autonomous machine action.</b><br>The gerund phrase “determining liability” is singular and takes “has become.”<br>Liability has become complex and ambiguous as a consequence of autonomous actions.<br>“Become” lacks agreement, “becoming” is non-finite, and simple “becomes” is less precise here.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): has become.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000074260","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"In the following question, a sentence with a blank is given, followed by five words labeled (1), (2), (3), (4), and (5). Choose the word that fills the blank appropriately in the context of the passage.<br><br>The rapid proliferation of artificial intelligence (AI) technologies (1)___ profound ethical quandaries, necessitating an urgent reevaluation of longstanding moral frameworks. While AI has demonstrably enhanced efficiency across industries, its deployment (2)___ contentious debates surrounding privacy, accountability, and autonomy. One critical concern is the opacity of algorithmic decision-making, wherein even developers may be unable to fully elucidate how outcomes are generated.<br><br>This phenomenon, often termed the “black box” problem, undermines (3)___ transparency, a principle integral to ethical governance. Moreover, AI systems trained on biased datasets risk perpetuating and even exacerbating systemic inequalities.<br><br>Compounding these challenges is the issue of agency: when machines perform autonomous actions, determining liability (4)___ complex and ambiguous. Beyond technical considerations, the ethical dilemmas posed by AI interrogate deeper philosophical questions about what it means to be human, to choose freely, and to coexist responsibly with non-human intelligences.<br><br>Thus, a multidisciplinary approach, encompassing philosophy, computer science, law, and sociology, is imperative to ensure that technological advancement remains (5)___ benign in its societal impact. Unless proactive governance mechanisms are implemented, humanity risks ceding essential elements of moral agency to entities whose operations it neither fully understands nor adequately controls.<br><br><br>The word “benign” most nearly means: (5) [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Harmful and destructive"},"2":{"en":"Beneficial and gentle"},"3":{"en":"Overly complex"},"4":{"en":"Artificially constructed"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Benign (सौम्य, हितकारी) = gentle, beneficial or not harmful.</b><br>Governance should ensure that technological progress has a benign social impact.<br>Harmfulness is the opposite; complexity and artificial construction are unrelated to benignity.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Beneficial and gentle.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000074261","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"Complete the following sentence in indirect speech with the correct option.<br>Kavyana said, “I am thirsty.”<br>Kavyana said that she ___ thirsty. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"is"},"2":{"en":"was"},"3":{"en":"had been"},"4":{"en":"will be"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Simple present becomes simple past after a past reporting verb.</b><br>“I am” becomes “she was.”<br>“Is” fails to backshift; “had been” unnecessarily uses past perfect.<br>“Will be” changes the time reference.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): was.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000074262","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"Choose the correct option to complete the sentence in indirect speech.<br>He said, “Have you ever been to the Marshall Islands?”<br>He asked me if I ___ ever been to the Marshall Islands. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"have"},"2":{"en":"had"},"3":{"en":"was"},"4":{"en":"would"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Present perfect becomes past perfect in reported speech.</b><br>“Have you been” becomes “if I had been.”<br>“Have” retains the original tense; “was” and “would” cannot form the required perfect construction.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): had.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000074263","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"Choose the correct direct speech transformation of the sentence.<br>Darci asked me if my father was at the office. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Darci said, “Was your father at the office?”"},"2":{"en":"Darci said, “Is your father at the office?”"},"3":{"en":"Darci asked me, “Is your father at the office?”"},"4":{"en":"Darci asked me, “Was your father at the office?”"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Restore the present tense in the original question and “my” to “your.”</b><br>“Was” becomes “is,” giving “Is your father at the office?”<br>A and D retain past tense; C unnecessarily repeats “asked me” inside the direct narrative.<br>B gives the appropriate direct question.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Darci said, “Is your father at the office?”.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000074264","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Complete the collocation by choosing a suitable word to fill in the blank.<br>Many professionals find it difficult to ___ a balance between work and personal life. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"keep"},"2":{"en":"strike"},"3":{"en":"set"},"4":{"en":"form"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Collocation: “Strike a balance between” means achieve a satisfactory compromise.</b><br>Professionals try to balance work and personal life.<br>“Keep a balance” is possible but less precise than the established collocation “strike a balance.”<br>“Set” and “form” are not idiomatic here.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): strike.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000074265","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct idiom for the word highlighted in bold.<br>This is so simple that even a <b>man in the street</b> can understand it. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A common or ordinary person"},"2":{"en":"A homeless person"},"3":{"en":"A wealthy businessman"},"4":{"en":"A police officer"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>The man in the street (आम आदमी) = an ordinary, average person.</b><br>The sentence means the idea is simple enough for anyone to understand.<br>Homelessness, wealth and police service are not implied.<br>The idiom concerns ordinariness, not physical presence on a street.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): A common or ordinary person.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000074266","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Phrasal Verbs","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with an appropriate phrasal verb.<br>The committee agreed to ___ the lesser clauses to prevent unnecessary complications. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"pare down"},"2":{"en":"pluck out"},"3":{"en":"plow through"},"4":{"en":"peel back"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Pare down (कम करना) = reduce or trim something.</b><br>The committee reduced the lesser clauses to avoid complications.<br><b>Pluck out (उखाड़ना)</b> = pull out abruptly<br><b>Plow through (पूरा पढ़ना)</b> = work through laboriously; <b>peel back (छीलना)</b> = remove a layer<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): pare down.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000074267","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Identify the word in this sentence that contains an error.<br>This information is irrelevant with our current topic. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"current"},"2":{"en":"irrelevant"},"3":{"en":"topic"},"4":{"en":"with"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Irrelevant” is followed by “to,” not “with.”</b><br>Correct sentence: “This information is irrelevant <b>to</b> our current topic.”<br>The erroneous word is “with.”<br>The remaining words are correct.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): with.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000074268","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Which of the given options arranges the following sentences in the most logical sequence to form a meaningful paragraph?<br>1. This groundbreaking finding has led archaeologists to reconsider the role of religious practices in shaping early human societies.<br>2. Recent excavations at Göbekli Tepe in Turkey have challenged conventional theories about the development of civilization.<br>3. The discovery of massive, intricately carved stone pillars suggests that organized religion may have preceded the advent of agriculture.<br>4. Previously, scholars believed that settled farming communities were necessary for the rise of large-scale social structures.<br>5. The site, dating back over 11,000 years, predates Stonehenge and the Egyptian pyramids by several millennia. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1-3-2-4-5"},"2":{"en":"3-4-5-2-1"},"3":{"en":"3-2-4-1-5"},"4":{"en":"2-4-3-5-1"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 2-4-3-5-1</b><br>Sentence 2 introduces the excavation, and sentence 4 states the older scholarly belief it challenges.<br>Sentence 3 gives the new religious interpretation; sentence 5 establishes the site’s age.<br>Sentence 1 concludes with the finding’s effect on archaeology.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 2-4-3-5-1.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000074269","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the parts of the sentence in the correct order.<br>The recent excavation<br>P. shedding light on lost civilizations<br>Q. dating back over two thousand years<br>R. with unique linguistic patterns<br>S. unearthed inscriptions and artifacts [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"QRSP"},"2":{"en":"SPRQ"},"3":{"en":"PSQR"},"4":{"en":"QSPR"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: SPRQ</b><br>S supplies the main predicate: the excavation unearthed inscriptions and artifacts.<br>P gives its historical value, and R describes the inscriptions’ unique linguistic patterns.<br>Q provides their age: over two thousand years.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): SPRQ.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000074270","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Which of the given options arranges the following sentences in the most logical sequence to form a meaningful paragraph?<br>1. It relies on measuring the decay of carbon-14, a radioactive isotope found in organic materials.<br>2. Carbon dating is a scientific method used to determine the age of ancient artifacts.<br>3. Despite its accuracy, carbon dating has limitations when applied to very old or non-organic materials.<br>4. Archaeologists use this technique to estimate the age of fossils, tools, and historical objects. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1-3-2-4"},"2":{"en":"2-1-4-3"},"3":{"en":"3-1-2-4"},"4":{"en":"4-2-1-3"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 2-1-4-3</b><br>Sentence 2 defines carbon dating, and sentence 1 explains its scientific basis.<br>Sentence 4 describes archaeological applications.<br>Sentence 3 concludes with the method’s limitations.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 2-1-4-3.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000074271","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct meaning of idiom:<br>Hung on his lips [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Argued relentlessly"},"2":{"en":"Was emotionally unstable"},"3":{"en":"Listened with deep admiration"},"4":{"en":"Spoke in riddles"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Hang on someone’s lips (बड़े चाव से सुनना) = listen with rapt attention or admiration.</b><br>Example: “The audience hung on his lips as he revealed the final secret.”<br>Relentless argument, emotional instability and riddles are unrelated.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Listened with deep admiration.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000074272","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Synonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate synonym of the given word: <b>OBFUSCATE</b> [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Explain"},"2":{"en":"Confuse"},"3":{"en":"Clarify"},"4":{"en":"Simplify"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Obfuscate (अस्पष्ट करना) = make something unclear or confusing.</b><br><b>Explain (समझाना)</b> = make clear<br><b>Confuse (भ्रमित करना)</b> = make difficult to understand ✔<br><b>Clarify (स्पष्ट करना)</b> = remove confusion<br><b>Simplify (सरल करना)</b> = make easier<br>More synonyms: obscure, cloud, bewilder.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Confuse.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000074273","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Find the part of the sentence that contains an error:<br>The management had the interns (1)/ to submit their reports (2)/ before the review committee (3)/ arrived for evaluation. (4) [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"(1)"},"2":{"en":"(2)"},"3":{"en":"(3)"},"4":{"en":"(4)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Causative “have + object” is followed by the bare infinitive.</b><br>Part (2) should read “<b>submit</b> their reports,” not “to submit.”<br>The structure is “had the interns submit.”<br>The remaining parts are correct.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): (2).</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000074274","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Change the following from active to passive:<br>The teacher had been praising the student. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The student had been praising by the teacher."},"2":{"en":"The student has been being praised by the teacher."},"3":{"en":"The student had been being praised by the teacher."},"4":{"en":"The student was being praised by the teacher."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Past perfect continuous passive = had been being + past participle.</b><br>The object “the student” becomes the subject.<br>A omits the passive auxiliary; B changes to present perfect continuous.<br>D uses past continuous rather than past perfect continuous.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): The student had been being praised by the teacher.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000074275","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Change the following from active to passive:<br>The company will refund the money. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The money is refunded by the company."},"2":{"en":"The money will be being refunded by the company."},"3":{"en":"The money will have been refunded by the company."},"4":{"en":"The money will be refunded by the company."}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Future simple passive = will be + past participle.</b><br>The object “the money” becomes the subject.<br>A uses simple present, B uses future continuous, and C uses future perfect.<br>Only D preserves the original future simple meaning.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): The money will be refunded by the company.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000074276","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Convert the sentence provided below from its passive voice structure to an active voice structure:<br>The manager is assumed to have had prior knowledge of the breach. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"It is assumed that the manager knew about the breach."},"2":{"en":"The breach assumed the manager knew it."},"3":{"en":"Prior knowledge of the breach is assumed for the manager."},"4":{"en":"The manager assumes knowledge about the breach."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Recast the passive perfect infinitive as a finite past-tense clause.</b><br>Option A preserves the assumption that the manager already knew about the breach.<br>B illogically makes the breach assume something; C remains passive.<br>D changes the manager into the person making the assumption.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): It is assumed that the manager knew about the breach.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000074277","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Convert the sentence provided below from its passive voice structure to an active voice structure:<br>Was the new protocol being tested when the issue was reported? [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Was the issue reporting the new protocol while it was tested?"},"2":{"en":"Was someone testing the new protocol when the issue was reported?"},"3":{"en":"Did the issue test the protocol during reporting?"},"4":{"en":"Was testing done on the issue because of the new protocol?"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Supply “someone” as the active agent and retain past continuous.</b><br>“Was someone testing the new protocol” is the active question.<br>A and C illogically make the issue perform an action; D changes the object and causal relationship.<br>The reporting clause remains unchanged.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Was someone testing the new protocol when the issue was reported?.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000074278","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Choose the most suitable option to replace the highlighted part of the sentence:<br>He is <b>capable to do</b> the task. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"capable of doing"},"2":{"en":"capable for doing"},"3":{"en":"capable in doing"},"4":{"en":"capable at doing"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Capable of + gerund” is the standard construction.</b><br>Correct sentence: “He is <b>capable of doing</b> the task.”<br>“For,” “in” and “at” do not follow “capable” in this pattern.<br>The gerund “doing” is required after the preposition “of.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): capable of doing.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000074279","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"A sentence is provided in indirect speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding direct speech.<br>He said that if it were not raining, they would go out. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"“If it was not raining, we would go out,” he said."},"2":{"en":"“If it were not raining, we would go out,” he said."},"3":{"en":"“If it didn’t rain, we would go out,” he said."},"4":{"en":"“If it were raining, we won't go out,” said he."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Restore “they” to “we” while retaining the hypothetical “were.”</b><br>The condition remains negative: “if it were not raining.”<br>A changes subjunctive “were” to “was”; C changes the construction.<br>D reverses the condition and changes the modal.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): “If it were not raining, we would go out,” he said.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000074280","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"In the following question, the first and last parts of the sentence (1 and 6) are given. The rest of the sentence is split into four parts and named P, Q, R, and S. These four parts are not given in their proper order. Read the sentence and find out which of the four combinations is correct.<br>1. Moisturisers for the face<br>P. as oily ones may block<br>Q. in greater concentration on the face<br>R. the oil glands found<br>S. should be chosen carefully<br>6. and cause pimple/acne to break out. [SSC CGL 14/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"RSQP"},"2":{"en":"PQRS"},"3":{"en":"SRPQ"},"4":{"en":"SPRQ"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: SPRQ</b><br>S supplies the main advice: facial moisturisers should be chosen carefully.<br>P explains why oily ones are risky.<br>R and Q identify what they block: oil glands found in greater concentration on the face, leading to part 6.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): SPRQ.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};